Titles: Lord of Mysteries, King of Space-Time, Beacon of Destiny, Embodiment of Sefirah Castle, Dominator of the Spirit World, The Hundred Human identity, The Truth concealed within the Mystery, The Rival of Deceit. The Fool Who Stepped Up, The Fool, Successor of the Celestial Worthy.
Honorific Name: Lord of Mysteries; King of Space-Time; Beacon of Destiny; Embodiment of Sefirah Castle; Dominator of the Spirit World (the original honorific name of the Celestial Worthy, inherited by Aletheia upon becoming the completed Lord of Mysteries).

Appearance: in Human Form, Aletheia possesses the appearance of a handsome young adult male with a slender physique, pale complexion, and slightly disheveled dark hair that falls naturally across his forehead. His facial features are refined, and his expression frequently conveys a quiet, almost enigmatic contentment. Following his fusion with the Celestial Worthy, his outward appearance became increasingly reflective of the symbolism associated with the Lord of Mysteries. He commonly wears elegant dark formal attire consisting of a white dress shirt, a fitted waistcoat, dark trousers, black gloves, and a long black hooded cloak with a distinctive golden interior. The cloak is decorated with intricate golden embroidery and mysterious ornamental patterns. Depending upon his manifestation, he may carry an ornate staff decorated with crystalline and celestial motifs. Despite his extraordinarily ancient subjective age, his preferred human manifestation retains a youthful appearance. As the Fool, during gatherings of the Tarot Club, Aletheia manifests as an ancient, mysterious figure seated at the head of a long bronze table within Sefirah Castle. His body is partially obscured by gray fog, allowing observers to discern his dark robes, golden embellishments, gloved hands, and general physical outline. However, his facial features remain indistinct regardless of how closely an observer attempts to examine them. He deliberately manipulates the perception of those attending the gathering, preventing them from perceiving aspects of his existence that would otherwise expose them to corruption. His manifestation gives off an incomprehensible yet tranquil impression. Rather than deliberately exerting divine pressure, he appears relaxed and content, creating the unsettling impression that the extraordinary environment surrounding him is merely an ordinary part of his existence. As the Lord of Mysteries, when manifesting greater portions of his divine nature, Aletheia is surrounded by boundless grayish-white fog, distorted spatial phenomena, celestial lights, and mysterious tendril-like extensions emerging from beneath his clothing. His appearance incorporates visual characteristics associated with both his original human identity and the Celestial Worthy. His black-and-gold garments bear a considerable resemblance to the manifestations adopted by his predecessor. Aletheia himself has humorously compared their resemblance to that of a parent and child possessing the same hereditary colour palette. As for Mythical Creature Form, the complete Mythical Creature Form of Aletheia has not yet been directly revealed. As the Lord of Mysteries, his existence encompasses the supernatural nature of the three Mystery Pathways, including Worms of Spirit, Worms of Time, and the corresponding mythical characteristics of the Door Pathway. An unrestricted revelation of his divine existence would be exceptionally dangerous to ordinary humans and lower-Sequence Beyonders. Consequently, Aletheia normally employs controlled manifestations, concealment, and perceptual limitations when interacting with lesser existences.

Personality: Before Becoming a Beyonder, Prior to his advancement, Aletheia possessed an expressive, humorous, irreverent, and occasionally reckless personality. His extensive metaknowledge of the supernatural world allowed him to approach otherwise terrifying circumstances with an unusual degree of familiarity. He frequently made jokes concerning dangerous Beyonder abilities, ancient existences, and the absurdity of supernatural advancement. His interactions with Amon were particularly characterized by provocative remarks, competitive behavior, and an apparent disregard for the enormous disparity between their respective levels of existence. Despite this behavior, Aletheia possessed a fundamental concern for human life. Upon realizing that Klein Moretti had seemingly never appeared or existed in this alternative existence, he chose to involve himself in the world's affairs rather than remain an uninvolved observer. His declaration of being the fool who stepped up originated from this period. After Becoming a Beyonder, Aletheia gradually became more experienced, cautious, and resourceful throughout his advancement along the Fool Pathway. Although his metaknowledge provided substantial advantages, his direct experiences with death, corruption, violence, isolation, and the loss of companions forced him to recognize the difference between possessing knowledge and genuinely understanding its consequences. His three hundred years of historical isolation further developed his patience and introspection. Nevertheless, he retained his characteristic humor and continued engaging in frequent verbal exchanges with Amon. His willingness to protect others remained one of the defining aspects of his humanity. As the Lord of Mysteries Following his prolonged struggle and eventual fusion with the Celestial Worthy, Aletheia became considerably calmer, more reserved, and more contemplative. The erosion of his humanity resulted in the gradual disappearance or weakening of many of his milder emotions. Experiences that would previously have provoked intense excitement, anger, fear, or amusement now generally produce restrained emotional responses. Although he remembers his former personality with considerable clarity, he cannot always reproduce the emotional significance associated with those memories. His present mannerisms frequently include faint smiles, quiet laughter, understated remarks, measured speech, and an almost perpetual appearance of contentment. Aletheia inherited numerous characteristics of the Celestial Worthy's divine nature, including His extraordinary cunning, patience, shamelessness, detachment, and affinity for deception. However, these characteristics remain directed by Aletheia's dominant consciousness rather than exclusively serving the original Pillar's selfish instincts. He possesses little desire to establish superiority through unnecessary displays of power. His confidence originates from an understanding of his actual capabilities, allowing him to remain composed even when confronted by the attention of multiple Outer Deities. Despite his emotional erosion, Aletheia continues to value companionship and ordinary human experiences. He particularly enjoys quiet conversations, drinking tea, taking leisurely walks, and resting in the company of individuals he trusts. His affection for such experiences is demonstrated by his willingness to spend considerable time within the Evernight Goddess's divine kingdom, where he openly requested her companionship and comfort shortly after awakening. Aletheia does not regard humanity as something that must become dependent upon his existence. Instead, he desires to preserve humanity's opportunity to live independently, believing that protecting individuals and controlling their lives are fundamentally different actions. His strongest remaining humanity manifests not through the intensity of his emotions, but through the significance he continues to assign to his choices and relationships 

History: Arrival and Encounter with Amon, Aletheia arrived in the Fifth Epoch as an ordinary human possessing extensive knowledge concerning the Twenty-Two Beyonder Pathways, their advancement requirements, ancient history, the Cosmos, and the identities of numerous Great Old Ones. Despite possessing information that would ordinarily expose an individual to severe corruption, Aletheia displayed an unexplained resistance to the consequences of forbidden knowledge. He eventually encountered Amon and established a peculiar relationship with the King of Angels. During their early interactions, Aletheia humorously challenged Amon’s reliance upon supernatural abilities to commit theft, claiming superiority after committing numerous instances of identity theft through ordinary means. He later created an extensive encyclopedia nicknamed the Beyonderdex, containing his accumulated knowledge of all Twenty-Two Pathways, potion formulas, acting principles, advancement rituals, and relevant historical circumstances. Through this knowledge, he informed Amon of the possibility of becoming a Dual-Pathway True God by replacing another individual during the latter’s apotheosis. The Fool Who Stepped Up, After discovering the apparent absence of Klein Moretti from the world’s history, Aletheia concluded that many events he remembered would no longer unfold as expected. Rather than attempting to directly imitate Klein’s identity, he decided to undertake his own journey. He subsequently consumed the Seer potion and advanced throughout the Fool Pathway. His experiences involved numerous supernatural confrontations, personal losses, near-death encounters, and moments of genuine happiness. He eventually became a Sequence 4 Bizarro Sorcerer, achieving demigodhood. Bargain with the Angel of Time, Upon encountering the advancement requirements of Scholar of Yore, Aletheia established a bargain with Amon. In exchange for assistance in advancing to Sequence 3 Scholar of Yore, Sequence 2 Miracle Invoker, and Sequence 1 Attendant of Mysteries, he agreed to provide Amon with knowledge regarding the circumstances and timing of Bethel Abraham’s return. With Amon’s assistance, Aletheia entered an isolated historical environment and experienced three hundred subjective years of separation from contemporary reality, successfully completing his Scholar of Yore advancement. He subsequently restored a forgotten historical settlement to the present era, fulfilling his advancement ritual for Miracle Invoker. During his preparation to become an Attendant of Mysteries, Aletheia and Amon confronted Zaratul and secured a Sequence 1 characteristic. Aletheia established a marionette town named Havenfall, assigning its inhabitants intricate individual histories, relationships, and destinies until the settlement developed a corresponding imprint within the Spirit World. He successfully advanced to Sequence 1. The Return of Mr. Door, Aletheia fulfilled his agreement with Amon by revealing the circumstances surrounding Bethel Abraham’s return and the intervention of the Mother Goddess of Depravity. He advised Amon to exercise restraint and wait for the decisive opportunity during Bethel’s apotheosis, rather than directly confronting the numerous True Gods and the Outer Deity involved. Amon subsequently replaced Bethel during the ritual, became Sequence 0 Error, and accommodated the corresponding Door authorities. Bethel’s final resistance against the Mother Goddess of Depravity allowed the arrangement to conclude without permitting Her descent. While assisting Amon, Aletheia secretly began preparing his own apotheosis. Apotheosis of the Fool, Aletheia acquired the remaining Attendant of Mysteries characteristics through arrangements involving Kotar and Antigonus. With assistance from the Evernight Goddess, he obtained the Fool Uniqueness and successfully performed an apotheosis ritual based upon Fooling History. He used the genuine historical circumstances of his existence to establish a conceptual contradiction in which history momentarily recognized him as an ancient deity returning to his former position rather than a newly ascending god. He successfully accommodated the Fool Uniqueness and the three necessary Sequence 1 characteristics, becoming Sequence 0: Fool. The Fool’s Gambit, Aletheia and Amon eventually reached Sefirah Castle, where their competing ambitions resulted in a confrontation over the position of Lord of Mysteries. Recognizing Amon’s reluctance to risk the permanent destruction of his individuality, Aletheia deliberately accelerated the awakening of the Celestial Worthy’s will. He presented Amon with two possibilities: continue competing and risk being replaced by the original Lord of Mysteries, or withdraw and potentially face the resurrected Celestial Worthy. Amon ultimately chose to retreat rather than wager his identity. Before Amon could escape, Aletheia combined Fooling and Grafting to manifest the effects of a supernova within Amon’s main body. Amon’s divine body was destroyed, allowing Aletheia to acquire the Error and Door Uniquenesses alongside their corresponding Beyonder characteristics. Amon subsequently resurrected through an avatar protected by Adam and departed into the Cosmos. The Fool’s Dream, Following his victory, Aletheia experienced an overwhelming awakening of the Celestial Worthy’s will. He entered the divine kingdom of the Evernight Goddess, where he fell into a deep slumber under her protection. Within his consciousness, Aletheia confronted the original Lord of Mysteries through an immense dreamscape constructed from memories, illusions, and competing divine authorities. The Celestial Worthy repeatedly attempted to erode his individuality, diminish the significance of his memories, and replace his consciousness. Their conflict continued for hundreds of thousands of subjective years, although approximately six years passed in the outside world. Eventually, Aletheia recognized that permanently eliminating the Celestial Worthy’s influence was not a viable outcome. He accepted their inevitable fusion and negotiated a compromise involving personal concessions, integration of their respective natures, and preservation of his dominant consciousness. Awakening as the Lord of Mysteries, Aletheia began awakening in stages, establishing connections between his consciousness and the outside world. Using his personal designation, The Fool Who Stepped Up, as a means of reinforcing his individuality, he broke the remaining illusions of the Fool’s Dream and forced the Celestial Worthy’s active will to retreat. He subsequently completed the accommodation of the three Uniquenesses, their corresponding characteristics, and Sefirah Castle. In 1358 of the Fifth Epoch, Aletheia fully awakened as the Lord of Mysteries. The Celestial Worthy’s will remained integrated into his existence, but Aletheia retained dominance over their shared consciousness. His awakening was immediately noticed by numerous Outer Deities beyond the Astral Barrier, who recognized both the return of the Lord of Mysteries and the familiar presence of the Celestial Worthy. Establishment of the Tarot Club, Following his awakening, Aletheia spent time recovering within the Evernight Goddess’s divine kingdom, discussing humanity, faith, the Orthodox Churches, and the events that had occurred during his absence. He subsequently returned to Sefirah Castle and deliberately summoned Audrey Hall and Alger Wilson, establishing the Tarot Club. Unlike Klein Moretti in the history he remembered, Aletheia possessed genuine divine authority from the organization’s inception and therefore had no need to impersonate an ancient deity. During the second gathering, he revealed the Acting Method and provided the two founding members with his five-line honorific name. He established protective arrangements allowing ordinary individuals to invoke his existence without being exposed to uncontrolled corruption. The Tarot Club currently gathers every Monday at three o’clock in the afternoon, Backlund time.

Overview: Aletheia is a Transmigrator, the founder and mysterious leader of the Tarot Club, and the current Lord of Mysteries. He is a Great Old One possessing the symbolism of a Pillar and complete authority over the Fool, Error, and Door Pathways, alongside full accommodation of Sefirah Castle. Originally an ordinary human possessing extensive knowledge of a possible history of the world, Aletheia became a Beyonder after discovering that Zhou Mingrui had seemingly never transmigrated into Klein Moretti. Recognizing that numerous individuals and civilizations would consequently be deprived of their intended protector, he independently undertook the Fool Pathway and pursued the position of Lord of Mysteries. He established an unusual cooperative relationship with Amon, exchanging knowledge concerning the latter's future apotheosis for assistance with his own advancement. Their cooperation ultimately developed into a rivalry over Sefirah Castle, culminating in Aletheia defeating Amon through a dangerous gamble involving the deliberate awakening of the Celestial Worthy's will. Following his victory, Aletheia entered a prolonged slumber under the protection of the Evernight Goddess. After enduring hundreds of thousands of subjective years of spiritual erosion and conflict against the Celestial Worthy, he reached a compromise with the ancient existence, accepting their inevitable fusion while securing the position of dominant consciousness. Although Aletheia successfully awakened as the Lord of Mysteries, the process irreversibly altered his personality and diminished much of his original humanity. Nevertheless, he retained his strongest personal attachments, fundamental values, and desire to protect humanity. He subsequently founded the Tarot Club in 1358 of the Fifth Epoch.

Trivia: Aletheia's name originates from the Ancient Greek alētheia, meaning truth. This is particularly ironic considering his authorities encompass deception, theft, mysteries, and the Fooling of reality. Unlike Klein Moretti, Aletheia established the Tarot Club after already becoming a completed Lord of Mysteries. Aletheia's earliest acquaintance among high-level Beyonders was Amon. His initial ambition to become the Lord of Mysteries originated partly from discovering the apparent absence of Klein Moretti. He experienced approximately three hundred subjective years of isolation during his advancement to Scholar of Yore. His conflict with the Celestial Worthy lasted hundreds of thousands of subjective years, while approximately six years elapsed in the physical world. Aletheia occasionally misses Amon despite having destroyed his main body with a supernova and is aware Amon subsequently resurrected through an avatar protected by Adam and departed into the Cosmos. He internally refers to the five-line honorific name of the Lord of Mysteries as our honorific name, acknowledging the Celestial Worthy's continued existence within their shared divinity. His preferred appearance shares the Celestial Worthy's black-and-gold colour palette. Despite possessing extraordinary authority over space-time, Aletheia enjoys walking at an ordinary human pace. Amanises is among the very few individuals to whom Aletheia has voluntarily revealed his true name. Aletheia has jokingly described the Celestial Worthy as an ancient father whose child inherited the family estate. Unlike his former self, Aletheia rarely raises his voice. His humor is now predominantly expressed through calm, understated remarks. His greatest ambition following his awakening is no longer advancement, but discovering how to live as the Lord of Mysteries without completely abandoning his remaining humanity.

RELATIONSHIP
Relationships: Despite being a completed Pillar and one of the highest existences within the Universe, Aletheia maintains a considerable interest in establishing and preserving relationships with other individuals, irrespective of their Sequence, status, or nature of existence. Although his ascension and subsequent integration with the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings have diminished certain aspects of his humanity, Aletheia has not entirely abandoned his former human sensibilities. He continues to find significance in companionship, conversation, curiosity, promises, and seemingly inconsequential experiences that an existence of his stature would ordinarily have little reason to pursue. His relationships are consequently characterised by an unusual balance between divine detachment and residual humanity. Through Morpheus Magsarion, Aletheia is capable of interacting with others without directly exposing them to his identity as the Lord of Mysteries, allowing him to establish relationships that are not entirely founded upon reverence, fear, or religious devotion.

Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings: Aletheia shares an extraordinarily complicated relationship with the Celestial Worthy, the previous Lord of Mysteries, whose consciousness and primordial will continue to reside within his existence. Initially, the Celestial Worthy represented the greatest threat to Aletheia’s individuality, possessing the potential to replace him entirely and resurrect through his body, characteristics, and connection to Sefirah Castle. During his confrontation with Amon, Aletheia demonstrated that he was willing to permit the Celestial Worthy’s resurrection rather than surrender his position and Sefirah Castle to his adversary. Following his prolonged slumber and an immeasurable internal struggle that encompassed hundreds of thousands of subjective years, Aletheia eventually reached an arrangement with the Celestial Worthy, resulting in their integration and his emergence as the completed Lord of Mysteries. Unlike a conventional resurrection, Aletheia retained his individuality and position as the dominant consciousness, while the Celestial Worthy continued to exist as an internally perceptible presence. Their relationship cannot accurately be described as either companionship or hostility. The Celestial Worthy is simultaneously Aletheia’s predecessor, former adversary, and an inseparable constituent of his current existence. Aletheia is capable of hearing the Celestial Worthy internally, even while conducting conversations and interacting with the external world. Their coexistence represents an extraordinary resolution to the conflict between the individuality of a newly ascended Great Old One and the primordial consciousness seeking resurrection through them. Nevertheless, their integration should not be mistaken for the Celestial Worthy’s unconditional submission or the complete disappearance of his original nature. Aletheia occasionally visits the Celestial Worthy within his own consciousness, engaging Him in conversations characterized by dry humor, philosophical disagreement, and mutual familiarity. He has jokingly described their relationship as resembling that of a parent and child, referring to their similar appearances, shared divine inheritance, and increasingly overlapping characteristics. Despite this unusual familiarity, Aletheia remains fully aware of the danger represented by the ancient Pillar.

Amon: Amon possesses one of the longest, most complicated, and personally significant relationships with Aletheia. Prior to their confrontation over Sefirah Castle, the two maintained a mutually beneficial relationship founded upon the exchange of knowledge and assistance. Their relationship originated when Aletheia was an ordinary human and Amon was already a King of Angels. Despite frequently insulting and provoking one another, they established a mutually beneficial arrangement that contributed to both individuals becoming True Gods. Amon assisted Aletheia with several of his advancements along the Fool Pathway in exchange for knowledge pertaining to his own future apotheosis. Aletheia subsequently assisted Amon in replacing the corrupted Bethel Abraham, contributing to Amon’s emergence as a dual-pathway True God of the Error and Door Pathways. Their cooperation eventually developed into direct opposition following Aletheia’s secret apotheosis as The Fool. During their subsequent struggle, Aletheia employed the Fool’s Gambit, demonstrating his willingness to relinquish his individuality to the Celestial Worthy rather than allow Amon to obtain Sefirah Castle. Their confrontation culminated in the destruction of Amon’s main body and the loss of his Error and Door Uniquenesses, alongside three Sequence 1 Worm of Time Beyonder characteristics. Amon nevertheless survived through an avatar protected by Adam, continuing his existence as a Sequence 2 Trojan Horse of Destiny. Despite their history, Aletheia does not regard Amon exclusively as a former enemy. He remembers their earlier cooperation and acquaintanceship, recognising that their confrontation, however consequential, does not encompass the entirety of their relationship. Following his awakening as the Lord of Mysteries, Aletheia eventually invited Amon to participate in the Tarot Club, granting him the unique designation of The Error, an unnumbered Arcana existing outside the traditional Major Arcana, which seemed appropriate for someone of his nature. Aletheia frequently finds Amon’s behaviour irritating, particularly his tendency to exploit ambiguities, manipulate circumstances, and interpret instructions according to his own amusement. Nevertheless, he remains sufficiently comfortable in Amon’s presence to engage in informal conversation and discuss matters that he would ordinarily conceal from other individuals, including his integration with the Celestial Worthy, his prolonged subjective experiences, and the nature of Morpheus Magsarion. Their relationship is no longer defined by competition over the position of the Lord of Mysteries, although Aletheia remains conscious of Amon’s inherently dangerous disposition. Upon admitting him into the Tarot Club, Aletheia explicitly instructed Amon to respect the privacy of its members, refrain from exploiting loopholes to harm them, and avoid attempting to parasitise Leonard Mitchell. Amon’s response to the final instruction was to innocently inquire as to who Leonard was. Their present relationship possesses elements of former rivalry, mutual curiosity, familiarity, and reluctant companionship. Amon is among the relatively few individuals capable of appreciating the extraordinary circumstances surrounding Aletheia’s ascension, while Aletheia remains one of the few existences capable of conversing with Amon without being particularly intimidated by his nature.

Amanises: The Evernight Goddess, Amanises, is one of Aletheia's most significant personal attachments and one of the few individuals before whom he willingly reveals his true identity and was an important ally during the most vulnerable period following his confrontation with Amon. She assisted his apotheosis, sheltered his prolonged slumber, and provided protection throughout his struggle against the Celestial Worthy. Following his awakening, Aletheia voluntarily sought her companionship, taking peaceful walks within her divine kingdom and requesting permission to rest upon her lap. He revealed his true name to her during one of these occasions. Aletheia particularly appreciates Amanises's composure, understanding, kindness, and willingness to interact with him as an individual rather than exclusively recognizing him as the Lord of Mysteries. Her presence possesses considerable personal significance to his remaining humanity. Their relationship is characterized by mutual trust, quiet companionship, sincere conversation, and occasional understated teasing. Although Aletheia’s subsequent completion as a Pillar placed him upon an entirely different level of existence, this development does not invalidate the importance of her earlier support. Her assistance consequently occupies an important position within his history, as Aletheia was unable to freely exercise the privileges of his newly acquired authorities without endangering his continued existence as an individual.

Tarot Club: Aletheia is the founder, patron, and presiding deity of the Tarot Club, an organisation whose members convene within Sefirah Castle every Monday at three in the afternoon. He interacts with its members under the identity of The Fool, ordinarily concealing his appearance and true nature beneath the gray fog. Unlike many deities, Aletheia does not demand religious devotion from the members of his organisation, nor does he require them to abandon their previous allegiances. Participation within the Tarot Club is voluntary, and its principles emphasise mutual assistance, equivalent exchange, personal privacy, and the prohibition of hostility between members. Aletheia has provided the members with considerable knowledge concerning the Beyonder world, including the Acting Method, potion digestion, advancement rituals, laws of Beyonder Characteristics and methods of communicating with his divine existence. By the eighth gathering, he had extended their advancement guides to Sequence 2, providing them with knowledge that could eventually permit them to attain Angelhood. Although the members generally regard Aletheia with considerable reverence, he does not exclusively perceive them as believers, subordinates, or instruments of his authority. Their individual personalities, ambitions, concerns, and experiences provide him with opportunities to remain acquainted with the comparatively mundane aspects of existence. Through their gatherings, Aletheia maintains a connection to individuals whose lives continue to possess uncertainties, aspirations, and difficulties that have become increasingly distant from his own existence as a Pillar.

Audrey Hall: Aletheia maintains a benevolent relationship with Audrey Hall, known as Justice within the Tarot Club. Alongside Alger Wilson, Audrey was one of the organisation’s two founding members and therefore among the earliest individuals to interact with Aletheia under his identity as The Fool. Audrey’s curiosity, enthusiasm, and developing understanding of human psychology distinguish her interactions with Aletheia. He has provided her with guidance concerning the Spectator Pathway, particularly the importance of distinguishing one’s genuine personality from the roles assumed through the Acting Method. Her presence within the Tarot Club represents a comparatively innocent and distinctly human perspective upon the supernatural world, contrasting considerably with Aletheia’s own experiences and accumulated knowledge.

Alger Wilson: Alger Wilson, known as The Hanged Man, was one of the original members of the Tarot Club. His cautious, pragmatic, and frequently calculating disposition distinguishes him from Audrey, particularly in his approach towards Aletheia’s identity and the extraordinary opportunities presented by the organisation. Aletheia provides Alger with knowledge and opportunities for advancement without demanding unconditional obedience. Their relationship consequently retains the characteristics of a beneficial arrangement between a mysterious divine patron and an ambitious Beyonder, although Alger’s understanding of Aletheia’s actual nature remains considerably more limited than the reality of his existence.

Derrick Berg: Aletheia acts as a divine patron and source of guidance to Derrick Berg, known as The Sun. Derrick’s circumstances within the Forsaken Land of the Gods distinguish his relationship with Aletheia from those of the other Tarot Club members, as the organisation provides him with access to knowledge and individuals beyond the severely restricted environment in which he resides. Through the Tarot Club, Aletheia provides Derrick with opportunities to acquire knowledge concerning his Pathway and the external world. Derrick’s sincerity and concern for his people contrast with the comparatively calculating motivations of certain other members, making his participation particularly distinct.

Fors Wall: Fors Wall, known as The Magician, maintains a relationship with Aletheia primarily through his position as the patron of the Tarot Club. He has provided her with knowledge concerning Beyonder advancement and the Door Pathway, alongside access to the organisation’s collective resources and assistance. The relationship is particularly significant from a metaphysical perspective, as Aletheia possesses the complete authority of the Door Pathway as one of the three constituent Pathways of the Lord of Mysteries. Fors consequently receives guidance from an existence whose understanding of her Pathway extends far beyond that of its ordinary practitioners, despite not possessing a complete understanding of his identity, Mr. Fool shows willingness to help her with issues concerning The Spirit World.

Emlyn White: Emlyn White, known as The Moon, participates in the Tarot Club while retaining his identity and affiliation as a Sanguine. Aletheia does not require Emlyn to abandon his existing loyalties in exchange for membership, allowing him to benefit from the organisation without surrendering his previous affiliations. Their relationship reflects Aletheia’s general attitude towards the religious and personal commitments of the Tarot Club’s members. Emlyn’s access to advancement knowledge and assistance is not contingent upon his conversion into an exclusive believer of The Fool.

Cattleya: Cattleya, known as The Hermit, possesses an unusual relationship with Aletheia due to having interacted with both his divine identity as The Fool and his manifestation as Morpheus Magsarion. Following her admission into the Tarot Club, Aletheia provided her with guidance concerning her circumstances involving the Hidden Sage and her prospective advancement. He explicitly permitted her to retain her loyalty to Bernadette Gustav, demonstrating that membership within his organisation did not necessitate the abandonment of her previous relationships. As Morpheus, Aletheia also travelled aboard Cattleya’s ship, the Future, interacting with her in the outward capacity of a wandering King of Angels serving The Fool. This allowed Aletheia to experience a considerably different relationship with Cattleya from that maintained within Sefirah Castle. Cattleya does not possess Aletheia’s complete understanding of the connection between these two identities. Consequently, she may distinguish between The Fool as her divine patron and Morpheus as an exceptionally powerful angel associated with him, despite both ultimately being manifestations of the same consciousness.

Leonard Mitchell: Leonard Mitchell, known as The Star, became a member of the Tarot Club during its eighth gathering. Aletheia provided him with the organisation’s established teachings, protected methods of invocation, and opportunities for advancement. Aletheia is particularly conscious of Leonard’s vulnerability in relation to Amon, owing to Leonard’s connection with Pallez Zoroast and Amon’s nature as a high-ranking Beyonder of the Error Pathway. Following Amon’s admission into the Tarot Club, Aletheia specifically prohibited him from attempting to parasitise Leonard. This precaution illustrates that Aletheia’s prohibition against harming fellow members is not merely ceremonial. He is willing to establish specific restrictions upon particularly dangerous individuals when their presence could threaten the continued safety of the organisation.

Xio Derecha: Xio Derecha, known as Judgment, was admitted into the Tarot Club alongside Leonard Mitchell during its eighth gathering. Aletheia provided her with the organisation’s teachings and advancement knowledge while permitting her to retain her personal ambitions and existing relationships. As with the other members, Aletheia does not demand unconditional religious devotion from Xio. Her membership represents an arrangement through which she may obtain knowledge, assistance, and opportunities for advancement while remaining responsible for her own decisions.

Bernadette Gustav: Through Morpheus Magsarion, Aletheia established a relationship with Bernadette Gustav, the Queen Mystic and daughter of Emperor Roselle. Their interactions possess particular significance due to Aletheia’s origins within the Pre-Epoch civilisation and his familiarity with the Chinese language employed by Roselle. During an encounter within a dream library, Morpheus revealed his ability to understand Chinese and subsequently began assisting Bernadette in learning the language. This offered her an opportunity to approach the private writings of her father through linguistic understanding rather than relying entirely upon external interpretation. Aletheia’s assistance to Bernadette was accompanied by explicit boundaries. Although Morpheus expressed a willingness to provide her with initial guidance, he cautioned her against excessively investigating his identity and the nature of his existence. Their relationship is consequently founded upon knowledge, restrained trust, and promises of assistance. Aletheia possesses information of considerable personal significance to Bernadette, yet he does not indiscriminately reveal everything within his knowledge. Through Morpheus, he approaches her as an enigmatic benefactor rather than openly presenting himself as the Lord of Mysteries.

Anderson Hood: Aletheia encountered Anderson Hood during his travels aboard the Future through Morpheus Magsarion. Despite possessing no particular obligation towards Anderson, Morpheus temporarily alleviated the effects of his curse, providing him with a degree of relief from his unfortunate circumstances. Their relationship represents one of Aletheia’s comparatively mundane interactions with the external world. Anderson is neither an established believer of The Fool nor an individual whose allegiance is necessary to Aletheia’s position as a Pillar. His encounter with Morpheus instead demonstrates Aletheia’s continued willingness to provide assistance to individuals whose circumstances happen to intersect with his own.

Ludwell: Ludwell, previously known as Admiral Hell, was transformed into a marionette by Morpheus Magsarion during his travels through the maritime regions. His vessel, the Black Tulip, and his Death-associated ring subsequently remained within Morpheus’s possession. Unlike Aletheia’s relationships with conscious individuals, his relationship with Ludwell is principally defined by the authority of the Fool Pathway over Spirit Body Threads and marionettes. Following his transformation, Ludwell ceased to participate in their interactions as an independently acting individual and instead became subject to Morpheus’s manipulation. As Morpheus is a direct manifestation of Aletheia, Ludwell ultimately exists as a marionette belonging to the Lord of Mysteries himself.

Humanity: Although Aletheia has transcended the conventional limitations of humanity, godhood, and individuality to an extraordinary degree, his relationship with humanity remains an important aspect of his existence. Having originally existed as an ordinary human, Aletheia retains memories and perspectives originating from a period in which he possessed neither supernatural authorities nor the privileges of divinity. His continued interest in ordinary experiences is particularly evident through Morpheus Magsarion. Rather than employing his manifestation exclusively for religious purposes, the elimination of adversaries, or the execution of divine arrangements, Aletheia frequently travels through the world for the simple purpose of experiencing it. During his voyage through the Sea of Ruins, he sought out mermaids and listened to their singing despite possessing no need to fulfil an advancement ritual. He approached them peacefully, played a flute, and protected their surroundings without seeking to acquire their Beyonder characteristics or exploit their existence. Such behaviour illustrates that Aletheia’s actions are not exclusively governed by necessity, authority, or the pursuit of greater power. Although his humanity has undergone considerable erosion, he remains capable of finding significance in experiences that offer him no measurable advancement or strategic benefit. For Aletheia, maintaining relationships with other individuals is therefore not solely a means of exercising divine influence. It is also a means through which he continues to experience existence as something more than the embodiment of the Fool, Error, and Door authorities.

SYMBOLISM 
Aletheia’s Authorities and Symbolisms: As the fully awakened Lord of Mysteries, Aletheia possesses the complete authorities of the Fool, Error, and Door Pathways, alongside the full accommodation of Sefirah Castle and the unique symbolism of a Pillar. His capabilities transcend the conventional authority of a Sequence 0 True God, allowing him to directly manipulate the higher-order symbolisms from which numerous supernatural authorities and Beyonder abilities originate. Through his inevitable fusion with the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings, Aletheia has inherited not only the original Lord of Mysteries' divinity but also His accumulated knowledge, instincts, experience, and extraordinary proficiency in manipulating symbolism. Although the Celestial Worthy's ancient will remains integrated into their shared existence, Aletheia retains the dominant consciousness responsible for directing these authorities. His existence stands Above the Sequence as one of the fundamental Pillars of the universe, representing the Spirit World and embodying the higher symbolisms associated with Space-Time, Destiny, Change, and the Inconceivable. Unlike a Dual-Pathway True God, Aletheia’s abilities are not merely the accumulation of authorities belonging to multiple Pathways, but the harmonious convergence of those authorities into higher forms of symbolism. His fusion with the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings additionally grants him access to the ancient existence’s accumulated knowledge, instincts, and understanding of mysticism, while Aletheia remains the dominant consciousness responsible for directing their shared divinity. Among the Great Old Ones, the Lord of Mysteries is particularly proficient in the application of symbolism, allowing Aletheia to utilize conceptual similarities, contradictions, and mystical relationships to produce phenomena that would otherwise be impossible. Nevertheless, his position does not grant unrestricted omnipotence, and his authorities remain subject to opposing symbolisms, the nature of convergence, and the fundamental principles governing the universe. The following descriptions distinguish Aletheia’s inherited canon authorities from their potential applications in your alternate universe, with each authority and symbolism presented as a continuous lore paragraph.

Pillar: Aletheia possesses the unique symbolism of a Pillar, representing one of the fundamental supports of the universe through his embodiment and dominion over the Spirit World, one of the three principal layers of existence alongside the Physical World and the Astral World. His status is not merely a quantitative accumulation of three neighbouring Pathways, but a qualitative convergence through which their corresponding authorities achieve a higher degree of completeness and mutual reinforcement. Although a Pillar does not belong to an entirely separate Sequence above ordinary Great Old Ones, its unique symbolism grants it a considerable advantage over them. Aletheia’s specialization in symbolic manipulation, ubiquitous manifestation, and the exploitation of mystical relationships allows him to contend with numerous opponents simultaneously, provided they do not possess symbolisms specifically capable of counteracting his methods. Furthermore, the will associated with his existence as the Lord of Mysteries cannot be permanently shattered in the same manner as that of an ordinary Great Old One, even through the intervention of another Pillar. This characteristic also explains why Aletheia could not permanently eliminate the Celestial Worthy’s ancient will and instead had to achieve dominance through their eventual fusion. Nevertheless, the indestructibility of this underlying will does not render Aletheia’s manifestation invulnerable, guarantee his continued dominance, or prevent him from suffering defeat.

Dominator of the Spirit World: As the Dominator of the Spirit World (灵界支配者), Aletheia embodies the symbolism associated with the Spirit World itself, granting him supreme dominion over its spiritual phenomena, mystical connections, information, inhabitants, and underlying structure. The Spirit World transcends conventional spatial relationships, allowing Aletheia to obtain information concerning events occurring in exceedingly distant Star Dominions without physically traveling to their locations, provided that the relevant information has not been concealed through sufficiently powerful means. He can mobilize the collective power of the Spirit World, employ it as an extension of his own divine existence, and temporarily deprive other beings of access to it on a universal scale. Consequently, supernatural abilities dependent upon the Spirit World, including certain methods of divination, spiritual communication, transportation, and supernatural perception, may become ineffective while his restrictions remain in place. Although sufficiently powerful Great Old Ones may resist or escape such restrictions under particular circumstances, entering the sealed Spirit World against his wishes is considerably more difficult. Through this symbolism, Aletheia possesses exceptional influence over the supernatural realm connecting numerous spiritual phenomena, mystical information, spiritual entities, divination, and extraordinary methods of travel. His relationship with the Spirit World extends beyond that of an existence utilizing it as an external medium, as its fundamental nature corresponds directly to his completed divinity. He can regulate access to the Spirit World, manipulate its connections with other regions, influence supernatural activities dependent upon it, and establish restrictions that interfere with the capabilities of other powerful existences. However, for the Lord of Mysteries who is capable of achieving Omnipresence state through Blink, Marionettes, Avatars, etc., as long as there is no Great Old Ones with specific symbols or abilities that counter his specialty, there is no fundamental difference between battling two, eight, or countless Great Old Ones. Even though Sefirot and Uniquenesses can only be used by one Marionette or Avatar at a time, he can still fight multiple opponents by relying on the Door Pathway to control various battlefields and then use Marionettes and Avatars in different battlefields to interfere and affect with his enemies. He would undoubtedly be able to hold off the Goddess of Fate, Supernova Dominator, Mother Tree of Desire (without the Source of Curses symbolism), and Circle of Inevitability on his own at the same time. While he might not secure a decisive victory, he would certainly not lose or allow his enemies disrupt other battlefields significantly. If the battlefield contained a single Great Old Dominator that could render the ubiquitous nature of Aletheia’s avatars ineffective, he would have to rely on his true body in combat, and could only leverage Pillar symbolisms while contending with an additional Great Old One. Unlike normal Great Old Ones who can have their will shattered—like how the Sefirot had their wills shattered by the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings and the Primordial God Almighty in the First Epoch—the will of a Pillar cannot be shattered, even by another Pillar. Aletheia can Seal the entire Spirit World across the whole universe, severing others' connections and influence over it, ensuring that for a set period, no creature can enter or utilize the Spirit World without Aletheia’s permission. This renders all abilities, authorities, and symbols related to the Spirit World ineffective, as well as blinding other creatures, including other Great Old Ones, to spiritual premonitions, making them unable to gather information from the Spirit World. Aletheia are able to utilize the power within the Spirit World to achieve different effects. The Lord of Mysteries can use the power of the Spirit World to allow subordinates to surpass their current characteristic level. This is similar to granting Boons. The upper limit that they could grant is a King of Angels level, this is the same way Spirit World Creatures get their power, level, and status. When fighting within the Spirit World, the Lord of Mysteries can generally mobilize the entire Spirit World's power to attack. If information is not hidden, as the Dominator of the Spirit World, he can theoretically see and know every piece of information within the Spirit World. The Lord of Mysteries can instantly receive information of the events happening in a different, significantly distant Star Dominion from the Spirit World. This lets him effectively shift his focus accordingly to any change in the battlefield. Through the convergence of the Spirit World with his other symbolisms, Aletheia possesses an extraordinary advantage in discovering secrets, manipulating mystical correspondences, and extending his influence throughout the Cosmos. His dominion over the Spirit World constitutes the foundation of his status as a Pillar rather than merely another authority he acquired through advancement.

Inconceivable (Bizarreness): Aletheia embodies the symbolism of the Inconceivable (不可思议), alternatively referred to as Bizarreness (诡异), representing phenomena whose existence cannot be adequately explained, comprehended, described, or reconciled with the established principles of reality. The symbolism originates from an aspect of the Original Creator, whose existence encompasses the exception to conventional understanding and comprehension. Through this symbolism, Aletheia can actualize circumstances that would otherwise be considered impossible, allowing contradictions, inexplicable transformations, and supernatural relationships to acquire genuine effects upon existence. Unlike ordinary manipulation, which operates through recognizable principles, the Inconceivable permits the realization of phenomena whose underlying processes cannot necessarily be understood through the laws they appear to violate. Its manifestations incorporate the combined foundations of Error and Miracles, elevating Change beyond understandable transformations into something fundamentally inexplicable. The Inconceivable additionally contains aspects of secrecy, concealment, and incomprehensibility, allowing Aletheia to obscure the nature of his existence and arrangements from other beings. Under appropriate circumstances, he can employ this symbolism to mitigate the effectiveness of opposing symbolisms, establish otherwise impossible mystical correspondences, and briefly draw upon a fraction of the Original Creator’s power. Nevertheless, the Inconceivable does not constitute unrestricted omnipotence, as its manifestations remain influenced by Aletheia’s status, the nature of the phenomenon, and the intervention of competing symbolisms. To encounter the Inconceivable is to encounter the possibility that an event which should never occur may nevertheless become an undeniable reality.

Change: Aletheia possesses the fundamental symbolism of Change (变化), granting him dominion over the transformations, transitions, developments, and alterations experienced by phenomena throughout existence. This symbolism encompasses ordinary transformations, erroneous transformations, and inconceivable transformations, incorporating contributions from all three Mystery Pathways rather than originating exclusively from a single authority. Through Change, Aletheia can influence the progression of a phenomenon, accelerate or decelerate its development, temporarily suspend its transformation, introduce abnormalities into its progression, or cause it to develop toward an alternative condition. Time itself falls within this symbolism, as its passage is intrinsically associated with the occurrence of Change. Consequently, Aletheia’s authority over temporal phenomena represents a manifestation of something more fundamental than conventional time manipulation. At its highest applications, Change can influence processes involving divine regeneration, accommodation, convergence, and the transformation of other Great Old Ones, although such intervention may require the full manifestation of Sefirah Castle and can encounter resistance from opposing symbolisms. Aletheia could have used Change to influence the Mother Goddess of Depravity's accommodation of the Brood Hive, but doing so would require full exertion of Sefirah Castle's power. When the Mother Goddess of Depravity was weakened after invoking the unique symbolism of the Chaos Primogenitor, Aletheia used Change to delay "Her" collapse into an embryonic state, while still being able to maintain the Astral Barrier and contend with the other eight Great Old Dominators at the same time. He caused immediate Change- an Error in the state of the erupting Supernovae from the Supernova Dominator's star-cluster form, causing them to collapse violently toward a single point. This threatened to create an unimaginably massive Black Hole. Aletheia could use Change to delay the awakening of the Primordial God Almighty's consciousness within Grisha Adam, allowing Grisha Adam to hold on a little longer. The distinction between Change and the Inconceivable lies primarily in whether the resulting transformation can be understood through an existing framework; when Change incorporates Error and Miracles to produce an inexplicable result, it approaches the domain of Bizarreness. Aletheia’s own transformation from an ordinary human into the Lord of Mysteries serves as a personal reflection of this symbolism, as his completed existence represents an irreversible transformation of both humanity and ancient divinity.

King of Space-Time: As the King of Space-Time (时空之王), Aletheia possesses the higher-order symbolism governing spatial and temporal relationships, including distance, position, dimensional boundaries, movement, temporal progression, and history. Originating from the broader symbolism of Change, this title signifies that Aletheia’s relationship with space-time is not restricted to manipulating individual locations or intervals; rather, he can influence the relationships through which locations, moments, and phenomena are distinguished from one another. He can traverse immense cosmic distances without conventional movement, alter the temporal conditions of entire regions, reposition astronomical objects, establish connections between otherwise separated dimensions, and interfere with the spatial and temporal abilities of other Great Old Ones. The King of Space-Time can influence phenomena on a universal scale, although other Great Old Ones possess overlapping symbolisms capable of contesting particular aspects of his dominion. Aletheia’s authority is especially formidable when combined with Grafting, Error, and Fooling, as the relationships between a target’s location, temporal condition, and corresponding history can be manipulated simultaneously. To Aletheia, distance is often little more than a relationship that can be altered, while the passage of time is a phenomenon whose progression can be negotiated through Change. Nevertheless, even the King of Space-Time remains subject to the universe’s inherent restrictions concerning the alteration of established history.

Beacon of Destiny: Aletheia embodies the symbolism of the Beacon of Destiny (命运道标), representing a guiding point within the River of Fate toward which the possible destinies of existences may be directed. Although manifestations of destiny appear throughout all three Mystery Pathways, the cornerstone of this symbolism is the elevation of the Door Pathway’s Position authority into the positioning of destiny itself. Through this symbolism, Aletheia can influence the direction in which numerous potential futures converge, causing a particular destination, encounter, or outcome to become the focal point of otherwise divergent possibilities. He can guide tributaries of the River of Fate toward a selected direction, manifest his presence within different temporal portions of destiny, and interfere with its progression by combining his symbolism with Change and the King of Space-Time. Rather than merely predicting a future, Aletheia can arrange the relationship between an existence and the destination toward which its fate is developing. His symbolism can oppose certain fate-related authorities, including aspects of Cycle and the predetermined progression of events, although it does not grant absolute ownership over fate and may enter direct symbolic opposition with existences such as the Goddess of Fate. The Beacon of Destiny is therefore fundamentally distinct from an unrestricted ruler of all destinies. Further accommodation of the Key of Light would elevate his dominion toward a more comprehensive control over fate, but would simultaneously threaten his stability through excessive convergence and proximity to the Original Creator.

Embodiment of Sefirah Castle: Aletheia is the Embodiment of Sefirah Castle (源堡化身), signifying that Sefirah Castle is no longer merely an external possession or source of borrowed power but an inseparable component of his completed existence. The true appearance of Sefirah Castle is an enormous bluish-black Door of Light composed of countless overlapping spheres of radiance containing transparent or translucent supernatural worms, from which grayish-white fog continuously emerges. The boundless space above the gray fog constitutes the divine kingdom accompanying the Sefirah, while the ancient palace and bronze table represent manifestations constructed within that domain. When Aletheia advanced to the Lord of Mysteries, the Fog of History spread throughout the World of Ruins, enveloping the entire planet and all living beings, while even spreading beyond the Astral Barrier into the boundless universe. Within the Fog, living beings either became dull-witted, filled with cunning, or inexplicably transported to the place they knew most intimately. In addition to that, numerous rules malfunctioned and many symbols were Fooled within the Fog. Aletheia directed the projection of the Bluish-Black Door of Light into the Protected Zones, where it scattered into countless starlit fragments, instantly transferring billions of humans, countless other species, and the scenes from the dream to a target planet at the edge of the universe. As its embodiment, Aletheia can directly mobilize its power, manifest its true form within the outside world, and employ it as the foundation through which his three Pathways achieve their complete symbolic convergence. When exercising the full extent of his Pillar symbolisms, Aletheia must manifest Sefirah Castle, which may appear as an immense Door of Light emerging from within the darkness of his black-and-gold garments. Through this manifestation, he can reinforce seals, isolate regions, transport vast populations, manipulate mystical connections, and enhance the effectiveness of his other symbolisms. Sefirah Castle additionally constitutes the foundation of numerous resurrection arrangements associated with his existence. As the Embodiment of Sefirah Castle, the Lord of Mysteries' Resurrection is, to some extent, limited to Sefirah Castle and the three corresponding Pathways, preventing him from reviving through other accommodated Sefirot. However, the symbolism of Inconceivable could allow him to bypass this limitation. Although the Sefirah is exceedingly difficult to truly damage, severe injuries inflicted upon it can weaken Aletheia for prolonged periods, and such damage does not necessarily disappear upon the resurrection of his physical manifestation. Accordingly, destroying one of Aletheia’s humanoid manifestations is fundamentally different from inflicting meaningful damage upon the Sefirah that constitutes his true divine foundation. The true body of the Lord of Mysteries, the Sefirah Castle, is almost impossible to truly harm. However, this does not mean there are no other ways to affect it. After all, even the Celestial Worthy ultimately fell.

AUTHORITIES 
Fooling: Aletheia possesses the symbolism and authority of Fooling (愚弄), representing the capacity to deceive the distinctions, relationships, definitions, and principles through which reality recognizes phenomena. Through this authority, he can blur the boundary between truth and falsehood, actuality and illusion, abstraction and substance, or historical phenomena and present existence. Rather than merely deceiving the perception of an individual, Aletheia can Fool the supernatural or conceptual conditions governing a phenomenon, causing reality to temporarily acknowledge a relationship that would otherwise be invalid. He can Fool History into recognizing a previously established condition as relevant to the present, Fool Time into accepting contradictory relationships between events, Fool Fate by obscuring the distinction between an intended destiny and its substitute, and manipulate the definitions governing supernatural restrictions. When combined with Grafting and Miracles, Fooling allows apparently fictional or imaginary phenomena to acquire tangible consequences. Aletheia can additionally employ Fooling to weaken the disadvantages associated with mystical contracts, although agreements witnessed by sufficiently powerful existences or Sefirot cannot necessarily be violated without consequences. This authority was fundamental to Aletheia’s apotheosis as the Fool, during which he deceived History into recognizing his ascension as the return of an ancient deity rather than the emergence of a new one. As the completed Lord of Mysteries, Fooling has become one of the principal instruments through which he manipulates higher-order symbolisms.

Foolishness (Blind Stupidity): Aletheia embodies the symbolism of Foolishness (痴愚), alternatively known as Blind Stupidity (盲目痴愚), representing the deterioration, suppression, and disruption of rational thought. Unlike Fooling, which principally manipulates the relationships recognized as true or valid, Foolishness directly influences the intellectual capacities through which a conscious existence evaluates its circumstances. Aletheia can diminish a target’s analytical ability, obstruct its judgment, reduce its awareness of contradictions, and cause it to undertake actions that it would ordinarily recognize as disadvantageous. Its influence may accumulate progressively, allowing an affected existence to continue believing that its decisions are entirely rational even while its capacity for reasoning deteriorates. When exercised at its fullest extent, Foolishness can temporarily reduce even a Great Old One to a state of profound intellectual stagnation, preventing it from recognizing developments or initiating deliberate actions. Nevertheless, existences operating primarily through instinct rather than conscious reasoning are comparatively resistant to this symbolism, while certain authorities associated with renewal and the regeneration of consciousness can counteract its effects. For this reason, Aletheia frequently combines Foolishness with Deceit, exploiting both the weakened judgment and remaining instincts of his opponents. The most terrifying aspect of Foolishness is that its victims may become incapable of recognizing the very process through which their intelligence is being diminished.

Error and Loopholes (Bug): Aletheia embodies the symbolism of Error and Loopholes (错误与漏洞), representing abnormalities, inconsistencies, exceptions, and exploitable defects within the principles governing existence. Through this authority, he can discover errors within supernatural arrangements, introduce contradictions into otherwise stable processes, exploit ambiguities within established restrictions, and cause phenomena to produce outcomes inconsistent with their intended operation. At its highest level, Error is not restricted to identifying preexisting weaknesses; Aletheia can actively participate in the creation of circumstances through which an exception becomes possible. Mystical contracts, identities, seals, divine kingdoms, supernatural abilities, and even the manifestation of opposing symbolisms may become vulnerable to the appropriate loophole. When combined with Fooling and Miracles, Error allows Aletheia to partially circumvent seemingly impossible conditions by altering the requirements or definitions through which a desired outcome is determined. However, this does not necessarily mean the original limitation has been completely removed; the resulting phenomenon may instead represent an alternative outcome that technically satisfies a modified interpretation of the desired effect. Error constitutes an essential foundation of the Inconceivable and represents one of the principal means through which Aletheia actualizes outcomes that ordinary supernatural principles would reject. His familiarity with Amon and subsequent fusion with the Celestial Worthy have further contributed to his extraordinary proficiency in recognizing how an apparently flawless arrangement may contain the foundations of its own failure.

Deceit: Aletheia embodies the symbolism of Deceit (欺诈), granting him the ability to mislead conscious existences, instincts, mystical connections, and the established rules governing phenomena. This symbolism extends beyond conventional lies and illusions, allowing Aletheia to manipulate the relationship between an existence’s intentions and the conclusions toward which those intentions lead. Rather than directly controlling a target’s consciousness, he may exploit its existing desires, ambitions, instincts, or incomplete understanding, causing it to voluntarily pursue an outcome that ultimately benefits his arrangements. Deceit can remain effective against existences whose behavior is governed primarily by instinct, making it particularly valuable when Foolishness proves insufficient. By combining Deceit with Error, Aletheia can cause supernatural rules to acknowledge interpretations contrary to their original purpose, while cooperation with Grafting permits him to redirect the mystical consequences of a phenomenon toward an unintended recipient. His proficiency is sufficient to make even other Great Old Ones vulnerable under favorable circumstances, especially when their fundamental instincts can be manipulated. However, the effectiveness of Deceit remains dependent upon the relationship between his arrangements and the target’s corresponding symbolisms. Aletheia’s personal irony lies in his possession of one of the greatest manifestations of deception despite bearing a true name associated with truth, and his deliberate restraint in using it against those who have willingly placed their trust in him.

Theft: Aletheia possesses the symbolism of Theft (窃取), originating principally from the Error Pathway and representing the forcible appropriation of properties, abilities, relationships, and conditions belonging to other existences. His authority encompasses not only physical objects but also intangible phenomena such as memories, thoughts, intentions, identities, concepts, lifespan, time, supernatural abilities, and destiny. At the level of a Pillar, Theft can temporarily affect certain symbolisms possessed by other Great Old Ones, although their most fundamental source symbolisms cannot simply be appropriated through this authority. Through its combination with the Inconceivable, stealing from a manifestation, avatar, or marionette may produce consequences affecting the original existence from which it originates, circumventing the conventional distinction between a substitute and its creator. Aletheia may appropriate the benefits of a supernatural arrangement, substitute one identity for another within a mystical process, or interfere with the relationship between a phenomenon and its rightful recipient. When supported by appropriate fate-related symbolisms, Theft can participate in arrangements involving the substitution of another existence’s identity and status within destiny itself. Nevertheless, the authority does not guarantee successful appropriation against every existence, particularly where opposing symbolisms or fundamental aspects of a Great Old One’s nature are concerned. Aletheia finds considerable amusement in possessing this authority, having once challenged Amon’s reliance upon supernatural theft while still an ordinary human.

Door: Aletheia embodies the symbolism of Door (门), representing the existence of passages, entrances, exits, thresholds, separations, and connections between otherwise distinct states or locations. The concept encompasses numerous subordinate authorities, including Space, Position, Sealing, Teleportation, and Alternate Worlds. Through Door, Aletheia can establish passages between the Physical World, Spirit World, divine kingdoms, remote cosmic regions, and concealed dimensions, provided that their corresponding restrictions can be overcome. A barrier that ordinarily separates two locations may be granted an entrance, while a previously accessible passage may be deprived of its corresponding exit. He can manifest numerous overlapping Doors around an existence, causing its attempts to escape to encounter successive layers of separation, each of which must be overcome before genuine freedom can be obtained. Conversely, Door allows Aletheia to withdraw from unfavorable circumstances by establishing a passage through boundaries that would otherwise restrict movement. When combined with Error and Decryption, he can discover or construct unconventional entrances within protected supernatural arrangements, while Fooling may cause a forbidden passage to be recognized as permissible. As the completed Lord of Mysteries, Aletheia’s mastery of Door signifies that conventional accessibility is rarely an immutable condition in his presence.

SUBORDINATE AUTHORITIES
Space: As a subordinate authority of the King of Space-Time and Door, Space grants Aletheia dominion over spatial relationships, distances, dimensions, directions, and the separation between physical and supernatural locations. He can compress or expand the distance between objects, overlap regions that ordinarily exist independently, isolate portions of space, and distort the dimensional conditions through which movement occurs. Rather than physically traversing the distance between two locations, Aletheia may directly alter their spatial relationship so that they become adjacent. This authority can additionally be employed destructively through the collapse, fragmentation, or distortion of spatial structures, producing phenomena of extraordinary intensity. When combined with Grafting, Aletheia can establish relationships between distant regions without requiring their conventional movement, while Door permits him to determine whether the boundaries separating those regions remain accessible. His application of Space is frequently understated, as demonstrated when he reduced the several metres separating himself from Amanises to a single metre without visibly moving from his original position.

Time: Aletheia possesses dominion over Time through the fundamental symbolism of Change and his position as the King of Space-Time. He can accelerate, decelerate, suspend, redistribute, or otherwise manipulate the temporal progression experienced by phenomena, interfering with the relationship between their development and the passage of time. By suppressing Change, Aletheia can cause temporal progression within a selected environment to approach stagnation; conversely, accelerating Change can cause an extraordinary amount of subjective time to pass within a comparatively brief external interval. His authority can interact with naturally occurring temporal distortions, reinforcing or opposing phenomena associated with gravity and space-time. At the height of his power, his influence over Time can extend across the universe, although this does not establish him as its uncontested absolute ruler, since other Great Old Ones possess corresponding temporal symbolisms. Aletheia can additionally traverse space-time toward the past, but the inherent principles of the universe prevent him from permanently rewriting established history through such travel. This authority is especially formidable when combined with Theft, allowing him to appropriate temporal intervals, and Fooling, allowing him to deceive the relationships through which separate moments influence one another.

History: Aletheia possesses the symbolism and authority of History (历史), allowing him to perceive, access, manipulate, and manifest phenomena preserved within the Historical Void. Through his position as the King of Space-Time, he can retrieve historical information, summon past conditions into the present, and cause the Fog of History to descend upon the Physical World. He can return phenomena originating from History to the Historical Void, depriving historical manifestations of their temporary physical presence. Aletheia can also conceal segments of established history and superimpose an imagined historical narrative upon their corresponding manifestations, producing effects resembling the alteration of history without genuinely rewriting the original past. When combined with Fooling, historical conditions may temporarily be recognized as applicable to present circumstances, allowing past events to acquire renewed consequences. However, such manipulations can be detected by sufficiently powerful existences and remain fundamentally distinct from permanently changing events that have already occurred. History additionally provides Aletheia with access to the memories of his former human existence, although retrieving the information associated with those memories cannot necessarily restore the emotional significance they possessed before his fusion with the Celestial Worthy.

Historical Projections: Historical Projections represent a manifestation of the authority of History, through which Aletheia can retrieve and actualize information preserved within the Historical Void, temporarily granting historical phenomena a tangible presence in the current world. He can summon objects, individuals, environments, and previous conditions, allowing aspects of the past to participate in contemporary events. Due to his completed Pillar status, the range, duration, stability, and complexity of his projections vastly surpass those available to a Scholar of Yore. He may maintain historical manifestations for extraordinary periods or incorporate them into arrangements involving Grafting, Puppetry, and Miracles. Nevertheless, a Historical Projection does not automatically reproduce the complete underlying status of its original, particularly when attempting to manifest a Uniqueness, Sefirah, or phenomenon associated with the Original Creator. Historical Projections therefore cannot be treated as unrestricted duplication of every existence that has ever appeared. Aletheia occasionally employs this authority for considerably more ordinary purposes, such as manifesting objects associated with his former life, reconstructing forgotten environments, or recalling the appearances of people whom he has not encountered for centuries.

Position and Destiny Positioning: Aletheia possesses the authority of Position, originating from the Door Pathway and elevated through its convergence with the other Mystery Pathways. This authority allows him to determine, manipulate, and establish the position occupied by an existence within spatial and mystical frameworks. Through information obtained from the Spirit World and the connections between phenomena, Aletheia can locate individuals, objects, concealed regions, and supernatural arrangements across immense distances, provided that their locations are not protected by sufficiently powerful concealment. He can additionally alter the positional relationship between a target and its surroundings, causing phenomena that would ordinarily remain distant to become accessible. At the level of the Lord of Mysteries, Position develops beyond conventional location and becomes capable of influencing the position occupied by an existence within destiny itself, forming the cornerstone of the Beacon of Destiny. Consequently, Aletheia’s mastery of Position allows him to concern himself not merely with where something presently exists, but also with the destination toward which its fate is developing.

Alternate Worlds: Aletheia possesses the authority over Alternate Worlds, originating from the broader symbolism of Door and its associated dominion over spatial boundaries. He can establish independent or isolated spatial environments, create supernatural regions separated from their original surroundings, and construct domains whose accessibility is governed by conditions of his choosing. Such environments may exist independently of conventional physical distances, allowing Aletheia to contain phenomena, shelter individuals, or prevent external interference without physically removing the surrounding world. Through the combination of Alternate Worlds, Fooling, Grafting, and Miracles, these domains can possess unusual relationships with reality, allowing their internal conditions to differ considerably from those governing their external environment. Nevertheless, the authority should not be confused with unrestricted creation of independent timelines or an infinite multiverse, as the established Door symbolism primarily concerns spatial and mystical separation. Aletheia can employ this authority to construct sanctuaries in which lesser existences can safely interact with his manifestations without being directly exposed to the full nature of his divinity.

Teleportation and Blink: Aletheia possesses extraordinary transportation capabilities derived from the Door Pathway, the King of Space-Time, and his dominion over the Spirit World. He can instantaneously reposition himself across enormous cosmic distances, manifest within otherwise inaccessible regions, and selectively transfer countless existences or objects to predetermined destinations. By employing Blink in conjunction with his other authorities, he can produce the practical impression of appearing simultaneously throughout numerous locations, leaving behind manifestations or afterimages that complicate attempts to determine his genuine position. He can transport entire populations or relocate consenting high-level existences without requiring conventional travel. Nevertheless, forcibly transporting an actively resisting Great Old One may require additional arrangements involving Sealing, Banishment, or symbolic suppression. Aletheia rarely considers physical distance an obstacle to social interaction, as demonstrated by his instantaneous traversal between Tenebrous Heaven and Sefirah Castle. Despite possessing such capabilities, he retains a personal appreciation for walking at an ordinary pace when accompanied by someone whose presence he enjoys.

Banishment (Exile): Aletheia possesses the authority of Banishment, allowing him to forcibly extract a target from its current location and relocate it to another spatial, spiritual, or historical environment. Unlike ordinary Teleportation, Banishment is principally concerned with removing an existence from a particular region against its wishes, depriving it of its ability to directly influence the circumstances from which it has been expelled. Aletheia can banish targets into distant cosmic regions, isolated spatial domains, or temporarily into the Historical Void. When confronting Great Old Ones, the effectiveness of this authority frequently depends upon his ability to restrict their movement or establish a corresponding Seal beforehand. Existences possessing powerful symbolisms of reality, dimensionality, or similar fundamental domains may resist the attempted separation from their current environment. Consequently, Aletheia generally employs Banishment as part of a broader arrangement rather than treating it as an unavoidable means of defeating every opposing existence.

Spatial Collapse: Spatial Collapse represents a destructive manifestation of Aletheia’s Space authority, through which he causes the spatial structure of a selected region to contract, fragment, or collapse. Rather than relying exclusively upon the release of physical energy, this application attacks the framework through which matter, energy, and phenomena occupy their corresponding positions. The resulting destructive effect may be concentrated within a comparatively restricted area while possessing an intensity capable of threatening exceptionally powerful existences. Through the combination of Spatial Collapse with Sealing and Grafting, Aletheia can restrict the affected region, preventing the phenomenon from unnecessarily extending toward unrelated surroundings. Nevertheless, opponents possessing appropriate gravitational, dimensional, or reality-related symbolisms may interfere with the manifestation. For Aletheia, Spatial Collapse is an expression of the principle that destruction need not originate from attacking an object directly when the spatial conditions permitting that object to exist in its present state can themselves be manipulated.

Space-Time Labyrinth: Aletheia can manifest a Space-Time Labyrinth through the combined authorities of Space, Time, Door, and his dominion over the Spirit World. This labyrinth consists of an extraordinary arrangement of overlapping spatial relationships, dimensional passages, and distorted temporal conditions, within which conventional navigation becomes insufficient. An existence attempting to escape may discover that its movement returns it toward a previously occupied location, that apparent exits lead deeper into the arrangement, or that the progression of time differs between corresponding regions. At the level of a completed Lord of Mysteries, such a labyrinth can temporarily imprison even a Great Old Dominator, although sufficiently powerful fate-related or dimensional symbolisms may provide alternative means of escape. The labyrinth becomes particularly formidable when combined with Foolishness and Deceit, as a trapped existence may become incapable of accurately recognizing the conditions responsible for its confinement. Aletheia can employ this manifestation to temporarily remove dangerous opponents from a confrontation without immediately attempting to destroy them.

Sealing: Aletheia possesses the authority of Sealing (封印), derived from the symbolism of Door and its dominion over the separation between existences. This authority allows him to restrict physical beings, spiritual entities, regions, supernatural phenomena, mystical connections, and certain abstract processes, preventing their influence from extending beyond established boundaries. He can seal targets within objects, isolate environments from external interference, obstruct supernatural communication, or suppress particular manifestations of an existence’s authority. His Seals can additionally incorporate arrangements that redirect or draw upon the power of a confined existence. When combined with Sefirah Castle, Aletheia can reinforce these restrictions through the status of a Pillar, allowing him to contain sufficiently weakened Great Old Ones through appropriate mediums. However, a complete Great Old Dominator possessing an intact consciousness, Sefirah, Uniquenesses, and corresponding characteristics cannot necessarily be perfectly sealed against its wishes. Aletheia also employs Sealing as a protective rather than exclusively restrictive measure, regulating the supernatural connections established through his honorific name and preventing uncontrolled aspects of his divinity from reaching ordinary worshippers.

Grafting (Reassembly): Aletheia possesses the authority of Grafting (嫁接), alternatively referred to as Reassembly (重组), originating from the convergence of Change and Bizarreness. This authority allows him to establish genuine relationships between phenomena that originally possessed no corresponding connection, including physical objects, locations, actions, consequences, abstract concepts, and supernatural authorities. Aletheia can rearrange the relationship between an event and its recipient, connect a distant phenomenon to a selected location, attach the consequences of an action to an otherwise unrelated existence, or combine separate conditions into a newly established supernatural whole. These relationships do not merely constitute illusions, as their successful manifestation produces tangible effects upon reality. Through its combination with Fooling, Error, and the Inconceivable, Grafting becomes one of Aletheia’s most versatile authorities, allowing him to actualize relationships that would ordinarily be considered impossible. His most notable application prior to becoming the completed Lord of Mysteries occurred during the Fool’s Gambit, when he Grafted the effects of a supernova onto Amon’s main body and employed Fooling to sustain the contradictory relationship. As a Pillar, Aletheia possesses a substantially greater proficiency in the manipulation of abstract relationships and symbolism through this authority, although sufficiently powerful opposing symbolisms can still interfere with or resist the resulting arrangements. 

Miracles: Aletheia possesses the authority of Miracles, representing the manifestation of wishes and phenomena whose realization surpasses conventional expectations or supernatural limitations. Miracles constitute one of the fundamental components through which Change develops into the Inconceivable, alongside the authority of Error. Through this authority, Aletheia can restore destroyed phenomena, answer wishes, reconstruct environments, actualize extraordinary circumstances, and influence events in ways that ordinary causality would not readily permit. By incorporating Fooling and Loopholes into a Miracle, he can reduce the conditions necessary for a seemingly impossible wish to achieve a meaningful result, although the resulting manifestation may represent a partial or modified fulfillment rather than the complete realization of its original intent. The greater the discrepancy between a desired phenomenon and the conditions governing its existence, the greater the importance of his other symbolisms in supporting its manifestation. Unlike his former existence as a Miracle Invoker, Aletheia’s completed status allows his Miracles to operate in conjunction with the full power of Sefirah Castle. Nevertheless, he does not regard wishes as unrestricted entitlement and generally refuses to fulfill requests that would deprive unrelated individuals of their freedom or impose disproportionate consequences upon humanity. His personal preference is to employ Miracles in ways that allow people to continue their own lives rather than making them entirely dependent upon divine intervention.

Resurrection: Resurrection (复生) constitutes a specialized manifestation of Miracles, representing the restoration of an existence following its apparent or actual death. As the completed Lord of Mysteries, Aletheia possesses extraordinarily advanced resurrection capabilities supported by Sefirah Castle, his Beyonder characteristics, the Historical Void, and the numerous arrangements available through Puppetry and Error. He can rapidly restore his existence following the destruction of a manifestation and exercise influence over the resurrection allowances associated with Miracle Invokers, including resetting his own corresponding limitations. His ability to distribute his presence through avatars and other manifestations further complicates attempts to permanently eliminate him. Nevertheless, Resurrection does not necessarily erase injuries inflicted upon the fundamental components of his divinity, nor does the restoration of his existence guarantee the preservation of his dominant consciousness under every circumstance. As the Embodiment of Sefirah Castle, his resurrection arrangements naturally correspond to his Sefirah and its associated Mystery Pathways, although the Inconceivable can potentially circumvent certain restrictions. Consequently, defeating Aletheia’s current manifestation is considerably different from preventing the eventual return of the Lord of Mysteries.

Puppetry: Aletheia possesses the authority of Puppetry (傀儡), a subordinate authority arising from the combined symbolisms of Bizarreness, Change, and the Dominator of the Spirit World. This authority represents the manipulation of existences through supernatural relationships that allow them to become extensions, substitutes, or instruments of his will. It encompasses the elevated applications of Marionettes, Spirit Body Threads Manipulation, Avatars, Parasitism, and related manifestations. Through Puppetry, Aletheia can simultaneously direct an extraordinary number of independently positioned manifestations, distributing his attention and supernatural influence throughout vast regions without requiring his primary consciousness to physically occupy each location. Even phenomena possessing immense supernatural status, including certain Uniquenesses, may become susceptible to applications of Puppetry under appropriate circumstances. His mastery of the authority allows the conventional distinction between himself and the instruments through which he acts to become increasingly uncertain. Nevertheless, opposing symbolisms capable of granting independent life, transferring damage between substitutes and their original, or forcibly drawing his genuine existence toward a selected manifestation can undermine this advantage. Despite the immense utility of Puppetry, Aletheia remains particularly cautious about employing it against ordinary humanity, having developed considerable discomfort with the manipulation of individual autonomy during his creation of Havenfall.

Spirit Body Threads Manipulation: Aletheia possesses complete mastery over Spirit Body Threads, allowing him to perceive and manipulate the supernatural connections associated with the spiritual structure and bodily control of living beings. At lower Sequences, the manipulation of these threads requires the gradual acquisition of control over a target; however, Aletheia’s completed Pillar status allows the process to be performed with extraordinary speed and on an immense scale. Through this authority, he can simultaneously interfere with the movements, bodily functions, and supernatural manifestations of countless individuals, converting suitable targets into marionettes through the establishment of complete control over their corresponding threads. When combined with his dominion over the Spirit World, the range and quantity of affected existences become practically incomprehensible to ordinary Beyonders. Nevertheless, high-level beings may resist through their own status, while certain opposing symbolisms can disrupt the relationship between a marionette and its controller. Aletheia generally refrains from employing this authority against innocent individuals, regarding the possession of the ability to control another person’s existence as fundamentally different from possessing the right to exercise it.

Marionettes: Marionettes are supernatural puppets created through Aletheia’s manipulation of Spirit Body Threads and the broader authority of Puppetry. Through these manifestations, he can extend his influence beyond his primary body, employ the corresponding abilities of controlled existences, and arrange innumerable independent points through which his will can act upon the world. His marionettes can operate at vast distances, participate in complex supernatural arrangements, and serve as substitutes or manifestations of his presence through the integration of his other authorities. As the Lord of Mysteries, Aletheia possesses the capacity to establish marionettes on a scale exceeding ordinary numerical comprehension, allowing entire populations to fall within his simultaneous control if he deliberately exercises the corresponding symbolism. However, marionettes remain vulnerable to authorities capable of severing their connections, granting them independent consciousness, or transferring consequences directly to their controller. Aletheia’s most significant personal experience with this authority occurred during the establishment of Havenfall, where he constructed an entire settlement of marionettes possessing elaborate histories, relationships, and individual destinies.

Avatars: Aletheia possesses the ability to create Avatars through the integration of the Error Pathway’s corresponding authority with Puppetry, the Inconceivable, and Change. These Avatars function as manifestations of his existence capable of operating across separate locations, undertaking independent responsibilities, participating in supernatural arrangements, and interacting with individuals without requiring the physical presence of his principal manifestation. Depending upon their constitution and the power assigned to them, his Avatars may possess considerable supernatural capabilities and represent authentic extensions of his authority. Aletheia can employ them to investigate the Cosmos, maintain seals, receive worship, and participate in multiple simultaneous confrontations. Their existence additionally provides numerous contingencies against the destruction of an individual body. Nevertheless, certain symbolisms can circumvent the distinction between an Avatar and its original, causing injuries, curses, or other supernatural consequences inflicted upon the former to affect the latter. Consequently, Aletheia does not regard every Avatar as an inherently expendable manifestation when confronting opponents of comparable standing.

Parasitism: Aletheia possesses the authority of Parasitism through the Error Pathway and its corresponding relationship with Puppetry. By employing Worms of Time, he can infiltrate the spiritual existence of a target, establish varying degrees of connection with its consciousness, interfere with its memories and perceptions, and potentially appropriate control over its actions or identity. The extent of Parasitism may range from concealed observation to the complete substitution of the host’s individuality, depending upon the nature and success of the arrangement. At the level of a Pillar, Aletheia’s mastery surpasses the ordinary applications associated with the Error Pathway, allowing even certain high-level supernatural phenomena to become potential recipients of parasitic influence. Nevertheless, the effectiveness of Parasitism remains dependent upon the target’s status, awareness, resistance, and corresponding symbolisms. Aletheia rarely employs this authority against those with whom he maintains genuine relationships, partly because his prolonged struggle against the Celestial Worthy has granted him an intimate understanding of the horror associated with another consciousness attempting to appropriate one’s identity.

Omnipresence: Through the combined application of Puppetry, Avatars, Marionettes, Blink, Parasitism, Historical Projections, Replication, and his dominion over the Spirit World, Aletheia can achieve a state of practical Omnipresence. Rather than possessing literal, unrestricted existence at every conceivable point in the universe simultaneously, he can distribute authentic manifestations of his presence across such an extraordinary number of locations that ordinary beings cannot perceive the limits of his simultaneous manifestation. Every Avatar, marionette, historical manifestation, or appropriately established spatial connection may become an avenue through which the Lord of Mysteries exercises his authority. This allows Aletheia to participate in numerous confrontations, observe developments across immense cosmic distances, maintain elaborate arrangements, and respond to multiple supernatural disturbances without relying upon the conventional limitations of a single physical body. In the absence of symbolisms specifically capable of counteracting such manifestations, engaging Aletheia with overwhelming numerical superiority may provide considerably far lesser benefit than expected. However, authorities capable of transferring consequences to his original existence, forcibly inducing convergence, or directly targeting Sefirah Castle can interfere with this state. His Omnipresence is therefore an extraordinary manifestation of the Mystery Pathways rather than an assertion of absolute omnipotence.

Replication (Recreation): Aletheia possesses the authority of Replication (再现), alternatively known as Recreation (重现), derived from the Door Pathway, the Spirit World, and the Inconceivable. This authority enables him to reproduce supernatural phenomena associated with other Beyonder Pathways, allowing him to manifest abilities and even certain authorities that do not naturally belong to his own three Pathways. At the level of a True God, the Door Pathway already possesses the capacity to replicate authorities corresponding to other Sequence 0 existences, and Aletheia’s completed Pillar status provides an even greater foundation for their application. Replication allows him to introduce otherwise unavailable supernatural effects into his arrangements without permanently accommodating the corresponding Beyonder characteristics. However, there remains a fundamental distinction between reproducing an authority’s manifestation and possessing the original higher-order symbolism from which it originates. Aletheia cannot simply replicate the essential symbolisms of another Great Old One and thereby acquire an equivalent divine existence. Consequently, Replication grants him extraordinary versatility without rendering the unique positions of other Great Old Ones meaningless.

Decryption: Aletheia possesses the authority and associated abilities of Decryption, originating principally from the Error Pathway and supported by his dominion over the Spirit World. Through Decryption, he can analyze mystical information, recognize concealed relationships, examine the structure of supernatural arrangements, and discover the principles responsible for phenomena whose operation would ordinarily remain incomprehensible. By combining his capacity for Decryption with Position, Door, and Error, Aletheia can identify concealed entrances, locate the foundations of complex Seals, and discover unconventional means of accessing protected supernatural domains. The authority additionally allows him to distinguish genuine mystical connections from misleading appearances and recognize opportunities for exploitation within opposing arrangements. Although Aletheia’s inherited knowledge from the Celestial Worthy provides an extraordinary foundation for this ability, Decryption does not grant absolute omniscience; information protected by sufficient Concealment or competing symbolisms may remain inaccessible. His mastery lies not merely in knowing a considerable amount of information, but in possessing the means to reconstruct the relationships necessary to understand something previously unknown.

Concealment (Secrecy): Aletheia possesses aspects of Concealment through the symbolism of the Inconceivable, specifically its association with the incomprehensible, the unknowable, and the secret. Through this authority, he can obscure information, conceal mystical connections, restrict supernatural observation, and prevent other existences from accurately perceiving the nature or location of a phenomenon. His Concealment may extend beyond ordinary invisibility, causing the information required to recognize an existence or arrangement to become inaccessible, indistinct, or incapable of being meaningfully interpreted. When combined with Fooling, Aletheia can allow observers to perceive an incomplete or misleading manifestation without realizing that their understanding has been deliberately restricted. When presiding over the Tarot Club, he employs this authority to conceal his facial features and dangerous divine properties while allowing his guests to perceive the general outline of his humanoid manifestation. Although Concealment constitutes an important aspect of his symbolism, it is not identical to the complete authority over Concealment possessed by the corresponding Darkness Pathway and its Above-the-Sequence existence. Aletheia’s manifestation of secrecy principally originates from the incomprehensible nature of Mysteries itself.

COMPOSITE APPLICATIONS & DIVINE CHARACTERISTICS
Symbolic Manipulation: As the Lord of Mysteries, Aletheia possesses extraordinary proficiency in the manipulation, interpretation, reinforcement, combination, and exploitation of symbolism. While ordinary Beyonders predominantly exercise supernatural abilities and True Gods embody corresponding authorities, Aletheia can directly influence the higher-order relationships from which many such authorities originate. Through Fooling, Grafting, Deceit, Error, and the Inconceivable, he can establish unconventional correspondences between symbolisms, strengthen existing mystical relationships, and cause a manifestation associated with one phenomenon to produce consequences upon another. This allows him to confront existences possessing greater direct destructive capabilities without necessarily opposing them through brute force. Rather than attempting to overpower an opposing symbolism through an equivalent manifestation, Aletheia may instead manipulate the conditions through which that symbolism becomes effective. Nevertheless, symbolic manipulation remains subject to countering relationships, differences in status, the fundamental nature of opposing existences, and the limitations of his own completed divinity. His proficiency distinguishes the Lord of Mysteries as an existence whose greatest strength lies not merely in the magnitude of his supernatural power, but in his extraordinary understanding of how power acquires meaning and produces consequences within the universe.

Realm of Mysteries: Aletheia possesses the Realm of Mysteries, the divine kingdom associated with the Fool Pathway, elevated through his complete accommodation of Sefirah Castle. Within such a domain, the conventional relationships between space, history, perception, identity, and physical phenomena may be extensively manipulated through Grafting, Fooling, and Concealment. Its internal structure does not necessarily correspond to the arrangement perceived by an intruding existence, as apparent entrances may lead toward unrelated environments, locations may possess concealed historical relationships, and seemingly genuine phenomena may conceal alternative purposes. Aletheia can establish manifestations of this divine kingdom within the outside world or employ the domain accompanying Sefirah Castle as his principal sanctuary. The Realm of Mysteries is especially formidable when combined with Error and Door, allowing him to manipulate the very conditions through which an intruder attempts to comprehend or escape its structure. Nevertheless, an existence possessing sufficient Decryption, symbolic status, or overlapping authority may discover methods of interfering with its arrangements.

Door of Light: The Door of Light is the true manifestation of Sefirah Castle and consequently the most significant external representation of Aletheia’s completed divine existence. Appearing as an enormous bluish-black Door composed of innumerable layers of spherical radiance containing supernatural worms, it symbolizes the convergence of the three Mystery Pathways and the Sefirah from which their corresponding Above-the-Sequence position originates. When manifesting the Door of Light, Aletheia can exercise the fullest extent of his symbolisms, using its presence to reinforce spatial and temporal manipulation, establish powerful mystical connections, strengthen Seals, and support the application of Change, Foolishness, and the Beacon of Destiny. The Door may emerge from within the shadows of his garments, appear throughout numerous regions through his distributed manifestations, or project portions of its radiance upon selected targets. Its manifestation represents the direct participation of Sefirah Castle in an arrangement rather than the ordinary use of Aletheia’s humanoid body. Consequently, the appearance of the Door of Light during a confrontation signifies that the Lord of Mysteries has begun exercising the full power of his completed position as a Pillar.

Authority over Mystical Connections: Through the combined symbolisms of the Spirit World, Position, Grafting, Fooling, and Deceit, Aletheia possesses extraordinary dominion over the mystical relationships linking individuals, objects, locations, authorities, and phenomena. Such relationships constitute the foundation of numerous supernatural processes, including divination, ritualistic magic, curses, prayers, symbolic manipulation, and spiritual communication. Aletheia can reinforce existing connections across immense cosmic distances, conceal or obstruct their manifestations, redirect their corresponding effects, and establish unconventional relationships through Grafting. He can additionally manipulate the distinction between the existence initiating a supernatural process and the recipient toward whom its consequences are directed. His control over mystical connections is especially significant in his dealings with the Tarot Club, as he deliberately regulates the relationships established between its members and Sefirah Castle. By controlling the manner in which these connections interact with his divinity, Aletheia allows ordinary individuals to communicate with him without requiring direct exposure to the otherwise dangerous nature of a Great Old One.

Divine Empowerment: As the Dominator of the Spirit World, Aletheia can provide subordinate existences with supernatural empowerment originating from the Spirit World’s power, allowing them to temporarily exercise capabilities surpassing the limitations of their existing Beyonder characteristics. Such empowerment operates similarly to a divine Boon, although its underlying foundation is associated with his dominion over the Spirit World rather than necessarily requiring the recipient to permanently accommodate additional characteristics. Under appropriate circumstances, Aletheia can elevate a subordinate’s effective status toward the level of a King of Angels. This application allows him to establish powerful emissaries, strengthen individuals entrusted with significant responsibilities, and provide temporary assistance during circumstances exceeding their conventional capabilities. Nevertheless, the empowerment does not automatically grant permanent ownership of the corresponding authorities, and its continued existence remains dependent upon the arrangements sustaining it. Aletheia generally prefers to provide assistance that complements an individual’s own development rather than replacing their advancement entirely with borrowed divinity.

Controlled Divine Revelation: Controlled Divine Revelation is an application developed by Aletheia through the combination of his completed authorities and retained humanity, allowing him to regulate the dangerous supernatural relationships established through knowledge of his existence. Ordinarily, sufficient information concerning a Great Old One can establish a mystical connection capable of exposing lesser beings to corruption, while direct perception of an unrestricted divine manifestation can produce devastating consequences. Aletheia deliberately employs Concealment, Fooling, Sealing, and his dominion over the Spirit World to restrict these connections, ensuring that individuals invoking his honorific name receive only the information and supernatural influence he intentionally permits. This allows him to reveal his complete five-line honorific name to ordinary Beyonders without deliberately subjecting them to the corruption associated with his true existence. His benevolence does not automatically eliminate the supernatural danger; rather, his goodwill motivates him to actively employ his authorities to prevent it. Aletheia additionally uses this application when interacting with the Tarot Club, creating controlled humanoid manifestations through which his guests can perceive his presence without directly observing the incomprehensible nature of the Lord of Mysteries.

Convergence of Authorities: Aletheia’s completed existence allows the authorities of Fool, Error, and Door to function as mutually reinforcing components of a single divine whole rather than as three independent collections of Beyonder abilities. Through this convergence, the limitations of an individual authority can frequently be addressed through the supplementary properties of another. An impossible Miracle may become achievable through Error; an invalid relationship may become meaningful through Grafting and Fooling; a concealed destination may become accessible through Decryption and Door; and an opposing destiny may become vulnerable through the combined application of Theft and the Beacon of Destiny. This extraordinary versatility constitutes the fundamental distinction between Aletheia and a conventional True God possessing only one Pathway. His fusion with the Celestial Worthy further enhances his understanding of these relationships, providing him with ancient knowledge concerning the manipulation of symbolisms. Nevertheless, this convergence does not exempt him from the Law of Beyonder Characteristics Convergence, the danger of accommodating additional Sefirot, or the continued influence of the ancient divinity integrated into his existence.

Symbolic Limitations and Counteractions: Despite possessing the status of a completed Pillar, Aletheia remains susceptible to opposing symbolisms capable of interfering with particular manifestations of his authority. Symbolisms associated with New Life and independent consciousness can undermine Puppetry and restore intellectual faculties suppressed through Foolishness, while those associated with Death, Decay, curses, and supernatural ravings may circumvent his distributed manifestations and directly affect their original existence. Convergence and Devouring can interfere with the separation between Aletheia and his Avatars, while powerful dimensional, gravitational, and reality-related symbolisms may obstruct his manipulation of Space-Time, Banishment, and Sealing. Similarly, his dominion over destiny can enter direct opposition with other fundamental fate-related symbolisms. Although the Inconceivable provides Aletheia with opportunities to mitigate certain disadvantages and establish unconventional alternatives, it does not automatically invalidate every countermeasure. Severe damage inflicted upon Sefirah Castle can additionally weaken his completed existence beyond the destruction of an ordinary manifestation. His most personal limitation remains the integration of the Celestial Worthy’s ancient will, whose influence cannot be permanently eliminated without disregarding the fundamental nature of their shared divinity. Consequently, Aletheia’s greatest advantage is not absolute invulnerability but his capacity to employ numerous overlapping authorities, allowing him to change his approach when one particular symbolism encounters effective 

Metaknowledge: Prior to becoming a Beyonder, Aletheia possessed extraordinarily detailed knowledge concerning the supernatural world, including information about events that had not yet occurred. His knowledge encompassed the Twenty-Two Pathways, potion formulas, advancement rituals, ancient historical events, the origins of numerous supernatural existences, and the identities and authorities of Great Old Ones. However, his knowledge represented a possible history rather than an infallible prediction of his own timeline. As his actions altered the course of events, its reliability concerning future circumstances gradually diminished. Meaning His original metaknowledge cannot reliably predict every event within a history that his own actions have substantially altered.

Resistance to Forbidden Knowledge: Even as an ordinary human, Aletheia demonstrated an unexplained ability to possess knowledge concerning numerous Great Old Ones without experiencing the immediate corruption normally associated with such information. The origin and full extent of this characteristic remain unknown. This resistance did not render him immune to the mental imprints within Beyonder characteristics or the awakening of the Celestial Worthy's will.

Fusion with the Celestial Worthy: Aletheia's completed existence incorporates the ancient will, memories, knowledge, instincts, and divine nature of the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings. Their relationship is fundamentally different from ordinary possession or parasitism. Both consciousnesses have undergone an extended process of mutual erosion and integration, resulting in an existence that cannot be described as entirely identical to either of their original forms. Aletheia maintains the position of dominant consciousness, directing the decisions and actions of the Lord of Mysteries. However, the Celestial Worthy's divine nature constitutes a substantial portion of their shared existence and continues influencing Aletheia's thoughts, dispositions, and perception of reality. Aletheia can voluntarily turn his awareness inward and encounter a manifestation of the Celestial Worthy within his consciousness, allowing the two to engage in direct conversations. Their relationship has developed from open hostility into an unusual coexistence characterized by mutual understanding, verbal exchanges, and occasional disagreement. The Celestial Worthy has not been permanently destroyed.

SEFIRAH 
Sefirah Castle (源堡): Sefirah Castle (源堡, Yuánbǎo), alternatively known as the Source Castle, the Castle of Origin, the Door of Light, and the Mysterious Space Above the Gray Fog, is one of the nine Sefirot left behind by the Original Creator on Earth and corresponds to the Fool, Error, and Door Pathways. Originally belonging to the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings, Sefirah Castle is presently fully accommodated by Aletheia, the current Lord of Mysteries, following his victory over Amon and the eventual fusion of his consciousness with that of the original Lord of Mysteries. Unlike an ordinary divine kingdom or a supernatural artifact, Sefirah Castle constitutes an inseparable component of Aletheia’s completed existence, providing the foundation through which the three Mystery Pathways converge into the symbolism of a Pillar. Although the Celestial Worthy’s ancient will remains incorporated within its current embodiment, Aletheia possesses the dominant consciousness responsible for directing its power.

Sefirah: Sefirah Castle is the Sefirah corresponding to the Lord of Mysteries group, possessing an intrinsic relationship with the authorities and symbolisms of the Fool, Error, and Door Pathways. As a legacy of the Original Creator, its existence predates the contemporary Beyonder system and cannot be adequately classified as a Beyonder characteristic, Uniqueness, Sealed Artifact, or conventional supernatural location. Aletheia’s complete accommodation of Sefirah Castle signifies that the Sefirah and his divinity have become components of a unified existence. Its significance is therefore fundamentally different from the relationship between a deity and an artifact under their ownership, as its power constitutes part of the very nature of the Lord of Mysteries. Through Sefirah Castle, Aletheia possesses the foundation necessary to exercise the combined symbolisms of the Dominator of the Spirit World, the King of Space-Time, the Beacon of Destiny, Change, and the Inconceivable at their completed level.

Embodiment of Sefirah Castle: Aletheia is the living embodiment of Sefirah Castle rather than merely its owner or administrator. Although he commonly manifests through a youthful humanoid appearance, that appearance does not constitute the entirety of his true existence. Sefirah Castle itself represents his fundamental divine body, while his humanoid manifestations provide convenient means of interacting with the outside world. The destruction of such a manifestation does not necessarily constitute the destruction of Aletheia, as the foundation of his existence remains associated with the Sefirah and the three Mystery Pathways. His relationship with Sefirah Castle also reflects the outcome of his struggle against the Celestial Worthy, since both consciousnesses now participate in the nature of the same completed Pillar, with Aletheia retaining authority over its direction. Consequently, when Aletheia refers to Sefirah Castle as belonging to both himself and the Celestial Worthy, he acknowledges their shared divine inheritance without relinquishing his dominant position.

Location Above the Spirit World: Sefirah Castle and its accompanying domain are situated above the Spirit World, occupying an extraordinary mystical position distinct from conventional physical space. Its location cannot be reached merely by traversing an astronomical distance. In antiquity, even Flegrea, the Annihilation Demonic Wolf, failed to enter it despite knowing of its existence. Lord of Mysteries Wiki +1 As its completed embodiment, Aletheia does not experience the same restrictions that once prevented prospective inheritors from accessing the Sefirah. He may move between its domain and the outside world through his own authority, without requiring an invocation ceremony or assistance from external anchors. To him, returning to Sefirah Castle is less a matter of traveling toward a distant location and more a matter of returning to the domain that constitutes an extension of his existence.

The True Sefirah Castle: Door of Light: The true appearance of Sefirah Castle is an enormous Door of Light possessing a bluish-black radiance. Its structure consists of innumerable overlapping luminous spheres containing transparent and translucent worm-like creatures, while an indistinct darkness lies beyond its threshold. The Door continuously produces grayish-white fog associated with the Historical Void. Fandom Within Aletheia’s completed existence, this Door represents the most authentic visible manifestation of his Sefirah and the convergence of the three Mystery Pathways. Although he ordinarily conceals it beneath his humanoid appearance, he may manifest the Door of Light within the shadows of his black-and-gold cloak, allowing its radiance to emerge from the depths of his garments. When fully revealed, the Door of Light signifies that Aletheia is directly mobilizing the fundamental power of his Sefirah rather than relying exclusively upon the individual authorities available through his humanoid manifestation.

The Boundless Gray Fog: The boundless gray fog surrounding Sefirah Castle constitutes an external extension of its existence and provides the environment within which its accompanying divine kingdom manifests. Its appearance resembles an immeasurable ocean of grayish-white mist, within which distance, direction, and the conventional passage of time possess little meaning to an ordinary observer. Although commonly treated as synonymous with Sefirah Castle, the gray fog is not the entirety of the Sefirah itself. For Aletheia, the fog functions as a medium through which he may express his authorities, obscure mystical phenomena, establish connections, and regulate the perception of those entering his domain. Its tranquil appearance conceals the extraordinary complexity of the symbolisms contained within it, including the capacity to interfere with cognition, spatial positioning, historical phenomena, and the rules governing supernatural processes. The density and visibility of the fog may be adjusted according to Aletheia’s intentions, allowing him to reveal selected portions of his domain while keeping its more dangerous aspects inaccessible.

The Historical Void: The Historical Void is a symbolic manifestation of history preserved within the Spirit World, possessing an intrinsic relationship with the grayish-white fog emanating from Sefirah Castle. Through his authority over History, Aletheia can access the historical information contained within this supernatural framework, retrieving past phenomena and allowing them to manifest within the present through Historical Projections. His complete accommodation of Sefirah Castle provides him with an exceptional foundation for manipulating the relationship between historical information and contemporary reality. Nevertheless, accessing a past event, reproducing its appearance, or superimposing its corresponding conditions upon the present remains fundamentally different from permanently rewriting established history. Aletheia occasionally employs the Historical Void for personal purposes, reconstructing environments associated with his former human existence and revisiting experiences that have become emotionally distant following his fusion with the Celestial Worthy. Although the Historical Void can preserve the information associated with those experiences, it cannot necessarily restore the humanity he possessed when originally experiencing them.

The Ancient Palace: The ancient palace within Sefirah Castle is a magnificent architectural manifestation constructed through the power of Wishes, characterized by an enormous dome supported by towering stone pillars. The palace is distinct from the Door of Light and does not constitute the Sefirah’s original physical form. In Aletheia’s alternate history, he maintains the palace according to the appearance he remembers from the history of Klein Moretti, regarding its architecture as an appropriate environment for contemplation, communication, and gatherings. Despite its majestic appearance, the palace exists principally for his convenience and can be altered according to his thoughts. Its enormous proportions and ancient atmosphere reinforce the impression that visitors have entered the residence of an incomprehensibly old existence. Aletheia, however, regards it with considerably less reverence, often using its throne room to drink tea, contemplate his memories, receive prayers, and enjoy the conversations of the Tarot Club.

The Bronze Table and Twenty-Two Seats: The principal hall of Aletheia’s palace contains an ancient bronze table surrounded by twenty-two high-backed chairs corresponding to the Major Arcana of the Tarot. The chairs are arranged symmetrically, with intricate patterns and unusual crimson constellations decorating their surfaces. The seat at the head of the table belongs to the Fool, from which Aletheia presides over the Tarot Club. Unlike Klein Moretti, who originally adopted the demeanor of an ancient deity to conceal his comparatively low Sequence, Aletheia occupies this position as the genuine Lord of Mysteries. His appearance during gatherings is that of a relaxed, contented figure wearing black-and-gold robes, with his facial features obscured through the deliberate manipulation of perception. The remaining seats are reserved for members of the Tarot Club, with Justice and the Hanged Man presently occupying the positions corresponding to Audrey Hall and Alger Wilson. Despite possessing the authority to compel obedience, Aletheia maintains the table as a gathering place where individuals may communicate voluntarily, exchange knowledge, negotiate assistance, and develop relationships independent of his direct control.

The Crimson Stars: The crimson stars scattered throughout the gray fog represent mystical connections to individuals in the outside world. Objects previously associated with Sefirah Castle can strengthen such connections and facilitate access to its domain. Lord of Mysteries Wiki Aletheia employs the crimson stars as convenient points through which he can establish communication, receive spiritual impressions, and invite individuals into his divine kingdom. The stars corresponding to Audrey Hall and Alger Wilson were utilized during the foundation of the Tarot Club and continue to serve as connections through which their spiritual representations may be summoned. Although Aletheia possesses the authority to investigate individuals through their mystical relationships, he generally refrains from unnecessarily examining their private thoughts and memories. When conducting a Tarot Gathering, he regulates the corresponding connections so that the members’ spiritual representations can safely enter Sefirah Castle without being exposed to the unrestricted nature of his existence.

The Transparent Cocoons: Suspended from the Door of Light by thin black threads are numerous transparent cocoons containing the preserved souls of individuals originating from the Pre-Epoch. These cocoons formed part of the Celestial Worthy’s arrangements for His resurrection, allowing selected individuals to be released into subsequent eras under suitable circumstances. Lord of Mysteries Wiki In Aletheia’s alternate timeline, the surviving cocoons represent remnants of his predecessor’s ancient designs rather than arrangements established by Aletheia himself. As the current embodiment of Sefirah Castle, he possesses the opportunity to inspect these remnants and determine how they should be handled. However, the absence of Klein Moretti’s canonical transmigration means that the precise number of opened cocoons and their corresponding occupants cannot simply be assumed to be identical to the original history. Whether Aletheia himself originally occupied one of these cocoons also remains unconfirmed. He regards the remaining souls as individuals rather than expendable instruments of resurrection, distinguishing his intentions from those of the Celestial Worthy.

