Avatar: Morpheus Magsarion is a high-ranking King of Angels of the Fool Pathway and a direct avatar of Aletheia, the Lord of Mysteries. Created following Aletheia’s complete awakening as a Pillar, Morpheus serves as a deliberately diminished manifestation through which Aletheia can personally experience and interact with the physical world without exposing its inhabitants to the overwhelming nature of His true existence. Despite possessing an authentic angelic constitution, genuine Sequence 1 Beyonder characteristics, and an apparently distinct identity, Morpheus is neither an independent individual nor a separate personality. His existence is comparable to a window through which Aletheia perceives and acts upon the world, while His true self remains within Sefirah Castle.

Appearance: Morpheus Magsarion takes the appearance of a tall, slender young man with a pale complexion, unruly black hair, and deep black eyes. His facial features are refined yet severe, possessing an austere beauty that gives him an impression of unnatural stillness. His eyes ordinarily display little discernible emotion, and his expression remains contemplative, solemn, or faintly melancholic. His disheveled hair falls irregularly across his forehead, occasionally obscuring one of his eyes. The contrast between his pale skin and predominantly black appearance accentuates the mysterious and almost spectral impression surrounding him. Although his human manifestation appears youthful, his mannerisms suggest an existence considerably older than his physical appearance would imply. His movements are measured and deliberate, his posture composed, and his gaze possesses an unsettling attentiveness that can make others feel as though they are being observed beyond their superficial appearances. Morpheus rarely smiles openly. On occasions when he experiences amusement or satisfaction, it generally manifests as a subtle change in his expression rather than an obvious display of emotion. His human appearance conceals the supernatural constitution of a King of Angels. Ordinary humans can perceive and interact with him without suffering corruption, provided he continues suppressing his angelic nature. Morpheus wears predominantly black garments resembling a combination of aristocratic formalwear, ceremonial robes, and an ancient ecclesiastical vestment. His principal attire consists of a long, fitted black coat with structured shoulders, a high collar, extended sleeves, and flowing lower garments reaching toward his ankles. The silhouette is narrow around his upper body before expanding into layered dark fabric, creating an appearance simultaneously dignified and ominous. His clothing possesses relatively little visible ornamentation. Unlike Aletheia’s black-and-gold divine robes, Morpheus’s attire emphasizes monochromatic austerity, with dark gray highlights and subtle variations in the texture of the fabric. When standing or walking, the lower portions of his garments frequently billow around him, giving his silhouette a distinctly spectral quality. He is occasionally accompanied by a black raven, which further accentuates his association with mysteries, omens, and the supernatural. The raven need not be a marionette; Aletheia may simply enjoy its company. The most distinctive feature of Morpheus’s appearance is his unusual mask. The mask possesses a rounded, elongated construction resembling an ancient helmet fashioned from dark metal and organic, bone-like materials. A prominent, oval-shaped black lens occupies much of its visible surface, surrounded by reinforced metallic rims and small engraved or riveted details. Extending downward from the lower portion of the mask is a long, segmented, vertebra-like structure, resembling an elongated breathing apparatus fashioned from a succession of skeletal components. When worn, the mask completely conceals his facial features and prevents observers from interpreting his expressions. Combined with his flowing black garments, it gives Morpheus an appearance closer to an ancient supernatural entity than an ordinary human Beyonder. The mask is particularly effective at distinguishing his public identity from Aletheia’s manifestation above the gray fog. It is not inherently a Sealed Artifact, nor is it the source of his supernatural abilities. Unless otherwise established, its function is primarily aesthetic and symbolic.

Persona: Morpheus Magsarion possesses a deliberately constructed persona assumed by Aletheia whenever He operates through the avatar. Although his consciousness, memories, knowledge, and fundamental intentions remain those of Aletheia, his outward temperament differs considerably from the Lord of Mysteries’ customary calm, contented, and occasionally playful disposition. Morpheus is an extraordinarily composed, taciturn, and contemplative individual who seldom displays unnecessary emotion. He conducts himself with the quiet dignity of an ancient sovereign, rarely feeling compelled to explain his actions or justify his presence to others.His speech is formal, measured, and occasionally philosophical. He seldom raises his voice, even when expressing displeasure or issuing a warning. His words frequently carry an implicit finality, making his statements appear more akin to declarations than suggestions. He possesses a preference for silence and solitude, often spending considerable periods observing his surroundings without speaking. His prolonged silences can become uncomfortable for others, although Morpheus himself finds them perfectly natural. Unlike Aletheia, whose quiet amusement frequently manifests through understated remarks and contented smiles, Morpheus maintains an almost perpetually solemn expression. His sense of humor is considerably drier, occasionally emerging through an unexpected observation delivered with complete seriousness. Morpheus possesses an immense sense of personal dignity and conducts himself with an aristocratic bearing befitting his status as a King of Angels. He dislikes unnecessary familiarity, excessive frivolity, and individuals who deliberately disregard established agreements. Although he does not ordinarily demand worship or reverence, he expects others to exercise a reasonable degree of courtesy. His pride rarely manifests through overt boasting. He considers the constant proclamation of one’s superiority unnecessary and occasionally beneath his dignity. When confronted by an arrogant individual, Morpheus generally responds through quiet indifference or a concise observation that exposes the insignificance of their pretensions. He can become particularly severe toward individuals who mistake his restraint for weakness. Nevertheless, his pride is part of the persona Aletheia deliberately maintains. It does not constitute an independent ambition capable of conflicting with Aletheia’s true intentions. One of Morpheus’s most prominent characteristics is his profound respect for responsibilities, promises, and agreements. Once he voluntarily accepts an obligation, he regards its fulfillment as a matter of personal dignity. He dislikes abandoning responsibilities merely because their completion has become inconvenient. He is particularly meticulous regarding supernatural contracts, promises of assistance, and the consequences of granting wishes. Morpheus does not necessarily fulfill every request presented to him, nor does he believe that possessing the ability to resolve someone’s predicament obligates him to do so. However, when he willingly promises his assistance, he makes considerable efforts to ensure that his words retain their significance. His relationship with duty occasionally makes him appear rigid or excessively formal, especially to individuals accustomed to Aletheia’s more relaxed temperament. Despite his distant demeanor, Morpheus is neither entirely indifferent nor incapable of compassion. He possesses Aletheia’s remaining humanity, attachments, and appreciation for ordinary existence, although he expresses these qualities through considerably more restrained behavior. Rather than openly comforting distressed individuals, Morpheus may quietly remain beside them, offer assistance without explanation, or resolve a predicament without demanding acknowledgment. He possesses a particular appreciation for stories, literature, dreams, memories, and the significance individuals attribute to their experiences. He finds it intriguing that ordinary humans can invest tremendous emotional significance into things that appear insignificant from the perspective of an Angel. His apparent coldness can occasionally conceal genuine consideration. Nevertheless, he is not particularly concerned with ensuring that others recognize his benevolence. He would rather perform an act of kindness and depart than remain to receive elaborate gratitude. Morpheus is extraordinarily difficult to provoke into visible anger. However, deliberate betrayal, the violation of important promises, or malicious interference with individuals under his protection can elicit a considerably more severe disposition. When angered, he does not ordinarily shout or engage in emotional outbursts. Instead, his speech becomes increasingly concise, his expression loses what little warmth it previously possessed, and his supernatural presence becomes considerably more oppressive. His punishments may possess a poetic or ironic quality, reflecting the Fool Pathway’s association with bizarreness, deception, mysteries, and the manipulation of reality. Nevertheless, Morpheus’s severity remains subject to Aletheia’s actual judgment. The persona cannot independently compel Aletheia to undertake actions contrary to His fundamental intentions. Morpheus Magsarion is not an alternative personality inhabiting Aletheia’s consciousness. His apparent individuality is an elaborate characterization consciously maintained by Aletheia. Every thought, decision, experience, and action undertaken through Morpheus ultimately belongs to the Lord of Mysteries Himself. Aletheia can discontinue or modify the persona whenever He wishes, although He generally maintains its consistency when interacting with others. Furthermore, the Celestial Worthy remains perceptible within their integrated consciousness while Aletheia operates through Morpheus. Consequently, Morpheus may appear externally silent and solemn while Aletheia internally engages in an unnecessarily humorous argument with the original Lord of Mysteries. This creates an extraordinary contrast between his outward appearance and his actual internal circumstances. Morpheus speaks with restrained authority, favoring deliberate, articulate statements over lengthy explanations. He rarely uses contemporary slang, exaggerated threats, or unnecessary expressions of emotion. His speech can occasionally possess a poetic or philosophical quality, especially when discussing human nature, history, fate, and mysteries. The following are original examples of his dialogue: When introducing himself: “Morpheus Magsarion. That is the name by which you may know me.”

ABILITIES OF MORPHEUS
Enhanced Spirituality: Morpheus possesses an extraordinarily developed level of Spirituality befitting a high-ranking King of Angels, granting him exceptional spiritual perception, intuition, mystical sensitivity, memory, and resistance to supernatural interference. His spiritual constitution allows him to simultaneously process numerous supernatural phenomena, perceive disturbances within his surroundings, and sustain multiple Beyonder abilities without experiencing the immediate exhaustion that would ordinarily affect lower-Sequence Beyonders. His extensive mystical knowledge originates not merely from his Beyonder characteristics, but also from Aletheia’s accumulated experiences and the ancient knowledge inherited through his integration with the Celestial Worthy. Consequently, Morpheus possesses knowledge considerably exceeding what would ordinarily be expected of an Attendant of Mysteries, although the supernatural strength through which he applies that knowledge remains deliberately restricted.

Spirit Vision: Morpheus possesses the ability to perceive spiritual phenomena ordinarily inaccessible to conventional human senses, including ghosts, specters, supernatural entities, spiritual disturbances, and the various aspects of an individual’s soul. Through observing these phenomena, he can acquire information concerning an individual’s physical condition, emotional state, spirituality, and the presence of extraordinary influences. Unlike lower-Sequence Seers, Morpheus can activate his Spirit Vision through intention alone, without requiring preparatory gestures. His perception can additionally be supplemented through his ability to observe Spirit Body Threads, allowing him to identify entities concealed through conventional supernatural invisibility. Nevertheless, sufficiently powerful Concealment authorities can obstruct his perception.

Divination Arts and Ritualistic Magic: Morpheus possesses exceptional proficiency in numerous forms of divination and ritualistic magic, including astrology, dream divination, pendulum divination, spiritual numerology, and scrying. Through these methods, he can obtain information from the Spirit World, investigate supernatural phenomena, determine the approximate location of individuals or objects, and perceive possible future developments. At his present Sequence, relatively simple divination procedures can produce revelations of considerable complexity, while Dream Divination can be performed without physically entering a state of sleep. His knowledge of mystical symbolism additionally allows him to construct, interpret, and modify supernatural rituals. However, his divination is not equivalent to omniscience, and revelations can remain inaccessible when obstructed by sufficiently powerful existences.

Danger Intuition and Spiritual Intuition: Morpheus possesses an exceptionally developed supernatural intuition that allows him to recognize impending dangers before their physical manifestation. Originally inherited from the Seer and Clown Sequences, this ability has undergone considerable qualitative development throughout the Fool Pathway’s higher Sequences. By combining spiritual intuition with divination, Morpheus can perceive potential future scenarios associated with himself or the subject of his investigation, allowing him to prepare responses before those circumstances occur. This ability is especially effective when detecting events that threaten his existence, although the accuracy of such revelations remains dependent upon the nature of the danger, the involvement of higher authorities, and the degree to which the corresponding information has been concealed.

Extraordinary Bodily Control: Morpheus possesses exceptional control over his physical manifestation, inheriting the agility, balance, coordination, flexibility, and precision characteristic of a Clown. He can deliberately regulate his posture, facial expressions, bodily movements, and physical reactions, allowing him to perform movements that would ordinarily exceed human anatomical limitations. His bodily control is further supplemented by his Shapeshifting ability and the spiritual constitution of an Attendant of Mysteries. Consequently, apparently involuntary expressions or physical reactions need not accurately represent his internal condition, making conventional behavioral observation an unreliable method of determining his intentions.

Drawing Paper as Weapons: Morpheus can temporarily alter the physical properties of ordinary paper, transforming otherwise fragile material into functional weapons. Originally manifested through the Clown’s Paper Daggers and subsequently developed through the Magician Sequence, this ability allows him to produce a variety of implements without requiring conventional manufacturing processes. The supernatural properties of the resulting objects are reinforced by his elevated Sequence and Spirituality. Although relatively insignificant compared with his higher authorities, this ability remains useful when Morpheus wishes to employ less conspicuous supernatural methods without revealing his actual level of existence.

Damage Transfer: Morpheus possesses the ability to displace injuries and harmful supernatural effects from their original location onto another suitable recipient or substitute. Initially manifested as the Magician’s ability to relocate wounds to less vulnerable portions of the body, Damage Transfer develops into a considerably more sophisticated ability at higher Sequences, allowing injuries, diseases, curses, and certain supernatural influences to be redirected into prepared Paper Figurine Substitutes. As an Attendant of Mysteries, Morpheus additionally possesses the higher authority of Reassembly, of which Damage Transfer can be regarded as a specialized subordinate application. Consequently, he can address harmful effects through both their immediate physical manifestations and, where his authority permits, the underlying connections responsible for transmitting them.

Flaming Jump: Morpheus possesses the ability to traverse distances through flames, allowing his manifestation to disappear into one source of fire and emerge from another. This form of transportation exploits properties associated with the Spirit World without requiring him to directly enter it in the manner of a Traveler. During the transition, he possesses temporary protection against the flames through which he travels. His ability to perform Flaming Jumps has been substantially enhanced by his higher Sequence, allowing him to traverse distances far exceeding those available to ordinary Magicians and to facilitate the transportation of objects through corresponding supernatural connections. Nevertheless, Flaming Jump remains distinct from the more advanced transportation achieved through Reassembly.

Flame Controlling: Morpheus can manipulate existing flames, ignite suitable materials, and produce supernatural flames through his own abilities. His control allows him to determine their movement and distribution within the effective range of his power, while simultaneously establishing suitable destinations for Flaming Jump. Although Flame Controlling is not equivalent to the fundamental authority over fire possessed by higher existences of the Red Priest Pathway, Morpheus’s spiritual constitution considerably enhances its effectiveness. He can employ fire as an instrument of misdirection, transportation, illumination, or supernatural offense.

Air Cannon: An extensively strengthened manifestation of the Magician’s Air Bullet, Air Cannon allows Morpheus to release concentrated projectiles of air through relatively simple gestures. The destructive force of these projectiles developed from the equivalent of conventional firearms at lower Sequences into artillery-like phenomena at the Saint level. As a King of Angels, Morpheus possesses a further strengthened manifestation of this ability and can deliberately regulate its output according to his intentions. Its precise maximum destructive capacity at his particular level has not been canonically quantified.

Paper Figurine Substitute: Morpheus possesses the ability to employ paper figurines as supernatural substitutes for himself or selected aspects of an individual’s existence. These substitutes can receive attacks, curses, divination attempts, tracking effects, and other hostile phenomena that would otherwise be directed toward their intended recipient. At higher Sequences, their applications extend beyond the replacement of an entire physical body, permitting the substitution of individual organs and the temporary preservation of normal bodily functions despite the absence of their original components. Through combining Paper Figurine Substitute with Reassembly, Morpheus can further manipulate the supernatural relationship between an original existence and its substitute, potentially preventing certain harmful effects from reaching their intended target.

Underwater Breathing: Morpheus can establish an invisible passage through which breathable air is conveyed to his manifestation while submerged beneath water. This ability originates from the Magician Sequence and has received substantial enhancement through his subsequent spiritual development. Although his present constitution allows him to overcome conventional physical limitations through considerably more sophisticated means, the inherited ability remains available to him when maintaining an apparently ordinary human manifestation.

Bone Softening: Morpheus possesses the ability to deliberately alter the rigidity of his skeletal structure, allowing his physical manifestation to escape conventional restraints or perform movements otherwise prohibited by human anatomy. This ability has become comparatively insignificant following his acquisition of advanced Shapeshifting and the interchangeable physical and spiritual constitution of an Attendant of Mysteries. Nevertheless, it remains an inherent component of his inherited abilities and can be employed without requiring a complete transformation.

Illusion Creation: Morpheus possesses the ability to construct highly convincing supernatural illusions capable of reproducing visual, auditory, and olfactory phenomena. These illusions can conceal individuals, objects, and extensive portions of the surrounding environment, reproduce conversations or movements that never occurred, and interfere with the perceptions and spiritual intuition of observers. The qualitative development of this ability at higher Sequences additionally permits the manifestation of illusory thoughts. Through combining Illusion Creation with Marionettes, Shapeshifting, historical manifestations, and Reassembly, Morpheus can construct circumstances in which numerous apparently independent phenomena originate from a single consciousness. However, his illusions do not inherently possess the unrestricted reality-altering properties of the Sequence 0 authority of Fooling.

Shapeshifting: Morpheus possesses extensive control over the appearance, structure, and arrangement of his physical manifestation. Inherited from the Faceless Sequence and subsequently enhanced through the Fool Pathway’s higher Sequences, this ability allows him to alter his facial features, voice, bodily proportions, skin, scent, and other identifying characteristics. He can transform into various creatures or reduce his manifestation into considerably smaller configurations of living flesh, subject to the corresponding limitations of the transformation. His ability to alternate between physical and spiritual states provides additional flexibility unavailable to ordinary Faceless Beyonders. Nevertheless, imitating the appearance of another Beyonder or Mythical Creature does not automatically grant Morpheus their corresponding authorities or Beyonder abilities.

Spirit Body Threads Manipulation: Morpheus possesses the ability to perceive, manipulate, and dominate the Spirit Body Threads corresponding to spiritual existences. Through these threads, he can directly interfere with the various components of an individual’s soul and indirectly establish control over their physical body. During the initial stage of manipulation, the target experiences increasing difficulty in performing physical movements and maintaining coherent thoughts, as their control over themselves gradually becomes obstructed. Upon completing the process, Morpheus transforms the target into a Marionette. At the level of an ordinary Attendant of Mysteries, complete conversion can be achieved within approximately three to four seconds under suitable circumstances. Morpheus’s possession of multiple Sequence 1 characteristics strengthens this authority further, although the exact improvement remains unquantified. The target’s Sequence, spiritual constitution, resistance, and external protection can influence the effectiveness of the process.

Marionette Creation and Manipulation: Morpheus can transform individuals whose Spirit Body Threads have fallen completely under his control into Marionettes, through which he can perform actions without directly exposing his principal manifestation. A Marionette retains the physical appearance, learned abilities, and Beyonder powers possessed during its original existence, allowing Morpheus to employ characteristics belonging to other Pathways indirectly without personally accommodating them. He can perceive the surrounding environment through his Marionettes, direct their movements, manipulate their speech, and utilize their corresponding abilities. Since their original spiritual condition is effectively that of deceased existences, conventional psychological manipulation is generally ineffective against them. However, their abnormal spiritual and fateful characteristics may permit sufficiently capable Beyonders to distinguish them from genuinely living individuals.

Marionette Interchange: Morpheus possesses the ability to instantaneously exchange his physical position with that of a Marionette under his control. Originally acquired through the Bizarro Sorcerer Sequence, this ability allows him to evade hostile phenomena, establish alternative positions, and obscure the location of his actual manifestation. He can additionally determine whether corresponding external objects accompany the exchanged bodies. Through combining Marionette Interchange with Reassembly, Morpheus can manipulate the spatial relationship between himself and distant Marionettes, effectively extending his operational network beyond the conventional geographical boundaries of the inherited ability.

Bestowal: Morpheus can separate Worms of Spirit from his Mythical Creature Form and implant them within his Marionettes, granting the recipients access to his corresponding Fool Pathway abilities in addition to those they originally possessed. These bestowed Worms of Spirit remain constituent parts of his existence rather than independent consciousnesses, allowing the Marionettes to function as distributed manifestations of his supernatural capabilities. At the Attendant of Mysteries level, his control over Spirit Body Threads becomes sufficiently sophisticated that he can additionally enable Marionettes to utilize his abilities without necessarily implanting a Worm of Spirit within them. This distinguishes his present degree of control from the conventional limitations of a Bizarro Sorcerer.

Distributed Spiritual Perception: Through his extensive network of Marionettes and Worms of Spirit, Morpheus can simultaneously perceive and interact with numerous locations while maintaining a unified consciousness. Rather than requiring each Marionette to possess independent intelligence, he can distribute his attention across them and employ their corresponding sensory capabilities as extensions of his own perception. The development of this network allows him to construct elaborate environments populated by apparent individuals whose actions, conversations, and interactions originate from his singular consciousness. Although an ordinary Miracle Invoker can already maintain thousands of Marionettes across an urban environment, Morpheus’s precise maximum capacity as a high-ranking King of Angels remains unspecified.

Regenerate: An ability exclusive to the Attendant of Mysteries Sequence and one of the more disturbing manifestations of its authority over Spirit Body Threads, Regenerate allows Morpheus to restore the historical Spirit Body Threads associated with materials that previously possessed a Spirit Body. Through this ability, substances originating from formerly living organisms can reacquire their spiritual connections and subsequently be transformed into Marionettes despite no longer possessing conventional biological life. Objects composed of materials that never possessed Spirit Body Threads cannot acquire them through this ability alone. Furthermore, the consumption of materials whose Spirit Body Threads have undergone this regeneration can transmit the supernatural influence to other organisms, potentially resulting in their transformation into Marionettes. Regenerate therefore extends Morpheus’s puppet-making authority beyond presently living targets and into the remnants of former life itself.

Historical Void: Morpheus possesses extensive authority over the Historical Void, the mystical domain containing the historical traces of existences, objects, and events. Through this connection, he can acquire assistance from his own past, manifest historical projections within reality, and temporarily withdraw his existence into the gaps of established history. His understanding of the Pre-Epoch and subsequent Epochs, supplemented by the knowledge inherited from the Celestial Worthy, provides him with an exceptionally extensive foundation for utilizing this domain. However, the Historical Void is not equivalent to unrestricted temporal manipulation, and his authority as an Attendant of Mysteries does not inherently permit him to rewrite events that have already occurred.

Historical Void Borrowing: Morpheus can temporarily draw strength from previous states of his own existence, restoring power and Spirituality that he possessed during earlier moments. This allows him to prolong supernatural activity and recover from circumstances that would otherwise leave his manifestation severely exhausted. The process can be repeated while sufficient Spirituality remains available to initiate the corresponding ability. Since Morpheus is a deliberately diminished avatar of Aletheia, his ordinary use of Historical Void Borrowing remains restricted to power appropriate to his manifested constitution. He does not automatically acquire the unrestricted power of the Lord of Mysteries merely because his controlling consciousness belongs to a completed Pillar.

Historical Projection Summoning: Morpheus can summon historical manifestations of individuals, objects, extraordinary artifacts, environments, and events with which he possesses sufficient familiarity. The effectiveness, duration, and authenticity of the resulting Historical Projection depend upon his understanding of the corresponding history, the relationship between himself and the subject, and the difference between their respective levels of existence. These projections can reproduce supernatural properties associated with their original counterparts, although manifestations of superior existences generally possess only a limited portion of their original power. Historical Projections ordinarily lack independent consciousness and rely upon instructions or instinctive behavior unless their corresponding consciousness directly assumes control. Morpheus can also manipulate their Spirit Body Threads, transforming suitable projections into Marionettes. However, Uniquenesses and existences inseparably connected to them cannot simply be reproduced in their entirety through conventional Historical Projection Summoning.

Historical Void Hiding: Morpheus possesses the ability to withdraw his manifestation into the Historical Void, concealing himself within historical gaps corresponding to periods and events he sufficiently understands. While concealed, he can direct his consciousness into a corresponding Historical Projection within the physical world, allowing him to remain operational without exposing his actual avatar body. His extensive historical knowledge grants him access to periods that would remain inaccessible to less knowledgeable Beyonders, potentially preventing them from following him despite possessing similar abilities. Nevertheless, remaining within the Historical Void consumes Spirituality, and ordinary withdrawal from it returns him to the corresponding physical location from which he entered unless supplemented by other supernatural methods.

Fog of History: Morpheus can produce supernatural fog and reduce the temperature of his surrounding environment, inheriting the atmospheric manifestations associated with the Scholar of Yore Sequence. These phenomena can accompany his applications of historical authority, concealment, and mystical transportation. Although visually reminiscent of the gray fog associated with Sefirah Castle, the fog produced through the avatar’s inherited abilities should not automatically be equated with the complete symbolism or unrestricted power of the Sefirah itself.

Miracles (Wishes): Morpheus possesses authority over Miracles, allowing him to fulfill wishes and bring about extraordinary phenomena that would ordinarily be impossible through conventional supernatural methods. The foundation of this ability originates from the Miracle Invoker Sequence, whose practitioners accumulate the capacity to perform particular miracles by repeatedly fulfilling corresponding desires. Through this process, Morpheus can produce effects involving restoration, transportation, alterations to environmental conditions, and temporary changes to an individual’s supernatural state. At the Attendant of Mysteries level, this authority undergoes further qualitative development, permitting more direct intervention in extraordinary circumstances. Nevertheless, wishes remain susceptible to distortion, particularly when their requested effects are excessively ambitious, ambiguously defined, or directed toward existences possessing superior divine status. Morpheus possesses the ability to directly manifest extraordinary phenomena through his authority over the Inconceivable, rather than being restricted exclusively to the conventional applications of his lower-Sequence abilities. He can achieve effects whose realization cannot readily be explained through ordinary supernatural principles, temporarily stabilize otherwise dangerous circumstances, and manifest phenomena originating from memories or historical experiences where the corresponding authority permits. As a high-ranking King of Angels, his manifestations of Miracles exceed those of an ordinary Miracle Invoker. However, his authority does not constitute unconditional omnipotence, and the realization of particularly ambitious miracles remains dependent upon accumulated power, preparation, supernatural status, and the nature of the desired phenomenon.

Resurrection: Morpheus possesses the inherent resurrection mechanism characteristic of the Miracle Invoker and Attendant of Mysteries Sequences. Upon the destruction of his manifestation, its Beyonder characteristics can return to the Historical Void and combine with historical Worms of Spirit, allowing a corresponding physical body to subsequently reform within reality. At Sequence 1, the conventional resurrection allowance is renewed, providing four resurrections independently of those previously expended at Sequence 2. The manifestation must ordinarily reform within three days and within the corresponding vicinity of its deceased body. Preventing the characteristics from returning to the Historical Void can obstruct the process. However, because Morpheus is an avatar rather than Aletheia’s principal existence, the destruction of his body or exhaustion of its conventional resurrection allowance does not inherently constitute the death of Aletheia. The latter could potentially reconstitute the manifestation through a separate act of divine intervention.

Jamming in Fate: Morpheus possesses a limited ability to influence the development of future circumstances, increasing or decreasing the probability of particular outcomes through supernatural interference with fate. This ability originates from the Miracle Invoker Sequence and represents a subordinate manifestation associated with the Beacon of Destiny. Unlike the direct manipulation of probability and fortune characteristic of the Wheel of Fortune Pathway, Morpheus’s influence operates through interference with the prospective development of particular circumstances. Although his elevated Sequence strengthens this ability, it remains distinct from the complete symbolism of the Beacon of Destiny possessed by Aletheia as the Lord of Mysteries.

Reassembly (Tampering/Grafting): Reassembly constitutes one of Morpheus Magsarion’s principal authorities as an Attendant of Mysteries, representing a preliminary manifestation of the Change and Bizarreness symbolisms. Through this authority, Morpheus can establish supernatural relationships between physical objects, existences, locations, events, and abstract concepts that ordinarily possess no direct connection, producing effects that are fundamentally real despite contradicting conventional logic. Rather than merely deceiving the senses or constructing an illusion, Reassembly alters the relationship through which the corresponding phenomena interact with reality. He can manipulate definitions, associations, orientations, and connections, effectively reorganizing the conditions governing a particular phenomenon. Conceptual Reassembly ordinarily requires an appropriate tangible subject to establish the intended direction of the alteration. The effectiveness of its application remains dependent upon the respective levels of the involved existences and their resistance to his authority. Through his authority of Reassembly, Morpheus can establish direct connections between geographically separated locations, effectively eliminating the necessity of traversing the intervening distance through conventional movement. These connections can extend between the physical world and suitably identified regions of the Spirit World, allowing him to achieve effects comparable to supernatural teleportation. Furthermore, he can manipulate the relationship between a distant Marionette and the effective range of his authority by Grafting its location onto another location within his immediate vicinity. Consequently, physical distance need not necessarily determine the limits of his Marionette network. His extensive knowledge of the Spirit World provides considerable advantages when determining suitable locations for these applications, although the avatar does not independently possess Aletheia’s unrestricted universal dominion over that realm. Morpheus can apply Reassembly to the abstract relationships underlying physical and supernatural phenomena, altering the manner in which their corresponding concepts are connected. For example, he can associate the beginning and endpoint of a physical route with the same position, causing an individual’s attempts to traverse it to return them to their point of origin. Through appropriately established connections, he can also redirect the intended recipients of supernatural phenomena, manipulate the relationship between an attack and its target, and interfere with certain mystical associations. These effects are not merely alterations to perception, but genuine changes to the corresponding conceptual relationship. Nevertheless, his authority remains that of a King of Angels and cannot unconditionally override the symbolism of superior divine existences. Morpheus possesses the ability to manipulate supernatural connections associated with prayers, Anchors, identities, targets, and other mystical relationships through Reassembly. By altering the destination or association of a corresponding connection, he can produce effects that would ordinarily require distinct supernatural abilities. This allows him to interfere with the transmission of hostile phenomena, redirect certain supernatural influences, and modify the relationship between an existence and its established substitutes. Such applications are particularly dangerous when combined with his knowledge of mystical principles, since Morpheus can recognize relationships that less experienced Beyonders may not even realize are present.

Realm of Mysteries (Concealment): Morpheus possesses the ability to manifest the embryonic form of the Divine Kingdom corresponding to the Fool Pathway, known as the Realm of Mysteries. This authority manifests through a combination of Concealment, spatial distortion, and the supernatural properties associated with Bizarreness, allowing Morpheus to isolate portions of his surroundings from external observation and interference. When engaged in important contemplation, an imperceptible curtain-like concealment can surround his manifestation, obstructing attempts by external existences to acquire information concerning his thoughts or activities. The Realm of Mysteries can additionally establish a degree of separation between an affected environment and the outside world, restricting the passage of individuals and information. Although formidable, Morpheus’s Realm of Mysteries remains the embryonic Divine Kingdom of an Attendant of Mysteries rather than the complete Divine Kingdom of a Sequence 0 Fool.

Physical and Spiritual State Interchange: As an Attendant of Mysteries, Morpheus possesses a spiritual constitution in which the distinction between his physical body and Spirit Body has become fundamentally ambiguous. Rather than possessing two conventionally separate aspects bound by ordinary biological limitations, his physical and spiritual manifestations can coexist, separate, and reintegrate according to his intentions. He can deliberately transition between material and spiritual states, allowing him to interact with circumstances that would ordinarily require an individual to abandon their physical body. This constitution represents a partial manifestation of the Fool Pathway’s relationship with Bizarreness and the Spirit World, further distinguishing Morpheus from conventional living organisms.

Mythical Creature Form: As a King of Angels of the Fool Pathway, Morpheus possesses a complete Mythical Creature Form fundamentally composed of Worms of Spirit. When his human manifestation is discarded, his physical constitution can reveal an aggregation of translucent, intricately patterned worms, forming writhing masses and tentacle-like extensions. These formations embody the supernatural principles of the Fool Pathway, particularly its relationship with the Spirit Body, spirituality, concealment and bizarreness. His humanoid appearance is therefore a controlled configuration of an angelic existence rather than a conventional biological body. Unlike an ordinary Bizarro Sorcerer or Scholar of Yore, Morpheus possesses complete control over the manifestation of his Mythical Creature Form under normal circumstances. Nevertheless, direct exposure to his unrestricted Mythical Creature Form can transmit dangerous supernatural information, producing madness, corruption, spiritual abnormalities, and potentially a loss of control in existences incapable of enduring his divine status. Morpheus therefore ordinarily conceals his Mythical Creature Form while interacting with humanity. His Mythical Creature Form remains distinct from Aletheia’s complete Pillar-level manifestation. Although both belong to the same underlying existence, Morpheus ordinarily expresses only the angelic symbolism of the Fool Pathway.

Worms of Spirit: The fundamental constituents of Morpheus’s Mythical Creature Form are countless Worms of Spirit, each representing a fragment of his spiritual and supernatural constitution. He can voluntarily separate these organisms from his manifestation, distribute them throughout his Marionettes, and subsequently retrieve them through their corresponding mystical connections. The Worms of Spirit remain extensions of his unified consciousness rather than individually autonomous personalities. They can additionally serve as suitable supernatural materials for the construction of high-level charms following appropriate preparation. However, the unnecessary destruction or permanent separation of substantial portions of his Worms of Spirit can damage the avatar’s spiritual constitution.

Extraordinary Regeneration: Due to his constitution as a complete Mythical Creature composed of Worms of Spirit, Morpheus possesses extraordinary regenerative capabilities that allow him to reconstruct damaged portions of his manifestation. Injuries that would permanently disable conventional organisms can be overcome through the reorganization and regeneration of his constituent spiritual organisms. Entire limbs and other extensively damaged portions of his apparent anatomy can be restored within relatively short periods. This regenerative capacity remains distinct from Resurrection, as it repairs an existing manifestation rather than restoring one whose corresponding existence has already been destroyed.

Distributed Mental Resistance: Morpheus’s consciousness is not dependent upon the integrity of a conventional human brain. Through distributing supernatural information and mental pressure across his numerous Worms of Spirit, he can mitigate certain forms of psychological interference, excessive knowledge transmission, and attacks directed toward his consciousness. His evolved constitution additionally reduces the effectiveness of certain Theft abilities employed against individual Marionettes containing his Worms of Spirit, since depriving an isolated manifestation of an ability does not necessarily deprive the principal avatar of that same ability. Nevertheless, equivalent or superior authorities can overcome these protections under appropriate circumstances, and his distributed consciousness does not constitute absolute immunity to mental or spiritual interference.

King of Angels Constitution: Morpheus possesses an authentic King of Angels-level spiritual constitution through the allocation of multiple genuine Sequence 1 Attendant of Mysteries Beyonder characteristics. Unlike manifestations whose extraordinary status originates exclusively from temporary bestowment or borrowed authority, his present level is supported by actual Beyonder characteristics belonging to the Fool Pathway. Consequently, the supernatural abilities inherited from its preceding Sequences undergo further enhancement beyond those of an ordinary Attendant of Mysteries. Although he has not accommodated the Fool Uniqueness within his avatar, his accumulation of multiple Sequence 1 characteristics satisfies the conventional criteria for classification as a King of Angels. His exact superiority over an ordinary Attendant of Mysteries remains dependent upon the corresponding distribution of characteristics and the circumstances of his manifestation. 

Unified Consciousness: Morpheus Magsarion possesses no independent personality, identity, will, or consciousness separate from Aletheia. His existence functions as an extension of the Lord of Mysteries, allowing Aletheia to directly perceive and interact with the physical world without requiring the descent of His principal divine manifestation. Every experience acquired through Morpheus is directly experienced by Aletheia, and every decision made through the avatar originates from the same controlling consciousness residing within Sefirah Castle. The relationship between them can be understood through the analogy of an individual looking through a window, wherein Morpheus constitutes the window rather than a separate observer. Consequently, the avatar cannot independently rebel against Aletheia, develop contradictory ambitions, or pursue succession to the Fool’s divine throne.

Integrated Celestial Worthy Consciousness: Due to Morpheus’s inseparable connection with Aletheia’s consciousness, the ancient will of the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings remains perceptible while operating through the avatar. The Celestial Worthy can observe the experiences acquired through Morpheus, communicate internally with Aletheia, and provide access to His accumulated knowledge and ancient understanding of mystical authorities. Nevertheless, this does not mean that the Celestial Worthy independently controls Morpheus or possesses a separate body within him. Aletheia remains the dominant consciousness governing their shared existence, and Morpheus’s actions continue to reflect Aletheia’s intentions.

Divine Concealment: Morpheus can deliberately suppress the manifestation of his angelic nature, concealing the dangerous information and spiritual influence associated with his complete Mythical Creature Form. By combining the Fool Pathway’s inherited Concealment abilities, Shapeshifting, and his exceptional control over his manifestation, he can interact with ordinary humanity while maintaining the outward appearance of a human individual. This allows Aletheia to participate in civilization without constantly exposing others to the unrestricted symbolism of the Lord of Mysteries. However, the revelation of Morpheus’s actual Mythical Creature Form remains inherently dangerous to ordinary individuals and lower-Sequence Beyonders.

Deliberately Diminished Manifestation: Despite possessing an inseparable ontological connection to a completed Pillar, Morpheus ordinarily exercises only those supernatural abilities and authorities appropriate to his genuine King of Angels constitution. His manifestation does not independently accommodate Sefirah Castle or the Uniquenesses of the Fool, Error, and Door Pathways, nor does it ordinarily exercise the unrestricted symbolisms of the Lord of Mysteries. The complete authority of Fooling, universal dominion over the Spirit World, and the higher symbolisms of the King of Space-Time and Beacon of Destiny remain associated with Aletheia’s principal existence. This restriction is deliberately maintained rather than imposed upon Aletheia by an external authority. Consequently, intervention from his principal existence would constitute the Lord of Mysteries directly exercising His authority through or upon the avatar, rather than an inherent demonstration of Morpheus’s ordinary King of Angels-level capabilities.
